{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas","id":169820,"title":"Share your Compact/ Conspiracy ideas!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-15T09:07:12-07:00","id":169820,"title":"Share your Compact/ Conspiracy ideas!","content":"Well, it was a matter of time before a thread like that would rise again, right?<br /> <br /> On my side, I've wrote <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/16573-conspiracy-raziel-ltd-wip\">Raziel Ltd</a> (an Israeli weapon company), the<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/38053-dying-conspiracy-ebony-fangs\"> Ebony Fangs</a> (an ancient death cult which hunts those who escape death) and I'm currently working on the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/139138-the-pythian-oracles-slashing-conspiracy\">Pythian Oracles</a> (slashers who kill for a better future). Plus, there are many ideas in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/125778-many-ideas-what-to-develope\">here</a>, which some I like more and some less. Finally, I lately thought about another &quot;werewolf based&quot; conspiracy:<br /> <br /> (temp name)- The Broken Diamond: a group of hunters which has found a number of crystal- like objects, which grant them spiritual powers when they transplant a part of that crystal into their flesh. The problem with those powers if that they disfigure the flesh of those who get the shards and turn them more bestial, and so they hunt after the werewolves in order to steal from them their secrets of flesh crafting. They don't know that those crystals are actually solidified form of the shards of the different Hosts, and that by using them they become more &quot;host like&quot; by themselves, with the only thing which keeps them &quot;human&quot; is the &quot;werewolf serum&quot;.<br /> <br /> P.S- just for convince, give each such group a temporary name if it is not developed enough. You can do a lot with a temporary name :P<br /> <br /> so what are your ideas? (and feel free to re-post old writeups of you =r old favorites!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T09:55:00-07:00","id":169863,"title":"","content":"I keep thinking that there needs to be a criminal compact somewhere, an organized crime group compared to the Night Watch (Who are more street level gang members) and Ascending Ones (Who are too mystical for my tastes). Something like the mob you see in the Sopranos or Godfather, or even a yakuza branch if you want to focus on Asia. Just something that really blurs the line even more between what's right and wrong in the Vigil, since a lot of monsters use criminals like disposable pawns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T10:30:46-07:00","id":169909,"title":"","content":"I had plenty of ideas during the years but may the God-Machine erase me if I can remember them now.<br /> <br /> Right now, the ones that are floating in my head are:<br /> <br /> - A Compact of esoteric architects that dates back to the Dark Ages (and possibly more) and hunts angels and demons with the idea that the secrets they hold can be used in their buildings and unlock the secrets of the universe<br /> <br /> - A Conspiracy (tentative names Wings of Icharus or Icharites) that hunts those who sin of hubris and try to defy the natural orders with their willpower and the excesses of science. Mostly a Promethean and Mage hunting group, I have <i>absolutely </i>no idea what their Endowment could be. Perhaps stolen advanced technology: highly hypocrital, but fits well with Hunter's greyness and a bit of &quot;fight fire with fire, even if it's wrong&quot;. I don't know much of Genius, but I suppose they would work well with it.<br /> <br /> I may have more to post once my memory starts to cooperate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 06-15-2014, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T11:12:27-07:00","id":169929,"title":"","content":"Pretty much every Hunter group, cannon or fannon, falls into one of three modes:<br /> <br /> 1) We come from this background, and want to protect people from this background. (E.G. The Union, Task Force: VALKARIE, Ascending Ones)<br /> 2) We dislike and kill a certain kind of monster (E.G. MM, The Long Night, Division VI)<br /> 3) We can profit from hunting and killing a certain kind of monster (Cheiron, LDI, Utopia Now)<br /> <br /> With around 30 different groups; I'm starting to get board of it and looking for other angles; in fact looking at my work, it's been leaning in that direction for a while. <br /> <br /> <br /> A Compact of therapist/actors who hire out to monster's unique needs - how much cash will an elder vampire pay to talk to a normal non-judging human about their lives in complete confidence that nothing can be used against them? Or what strange goblin wears could a Changeling pay for someone who can convincingly pretend to be their old family? Their Endowment comes from a True Fae, and guarantees their safety; and the safety of the secrets they're told.<br /> <br /> <br /> A group of exiles from, (maybe Lyonesse, Ys or Thuvaraiyam Pathi? There's no shortage of lost lands) who's only goal is to bring back their home. They're constantly reforging links between the far flung cells and tearing them down as groups go into hiding; or assimilate into their local culture. They have powerful Fetishes containing the Spirits of their homeland (River spirits, Hill spirits, etc), and their Endowment is based on the ability to remotely channel the Fetishes your Cell has. The Elemental Masteries could be used as inspiration here. The problem is that those powerful Fetishes are tempting to others.<br /> <br /> <br /> A group of honest to god knight errants who just go questing around doing good deeds. Maybe hunting monsters, but maybe just helping out at a natural disaster. Most people know them as a weird subculture. Their Endowment is Talecrafting, but they can only use Chivalric Romance troupes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T12:06:31-07:00","id":169969,"title":"","content":"@KingsRaven: Your last idea is a wandering group of modern bogatyr? I can dig it. As for my own personal ideas, I like mirrors to existing groups - things like a disavowed Soviet group similar to VALKYRIE, or a Chinese government agency that works like Cheiron, or the idea for an Orthodox equivalent of the Maleficarum - because I'm weird. Government sanctioned groups and corporations are my favorite types, so VASCU, VALKYRIE, and Cheiron cover a lot of bases for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T13:42:46-07:00","id":170092,"title":"","content":"Close. I'm thinking more Arthurian than Slavic. I'm British, sue me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Mirrors of existing groups, I would do it once - because to me &quot;amusing mirror of an existing group&quot; is a niche that hasn't been filled. But you like government sanctioned groups, well don't limit your imagination: TF:V are military, VASCU are law enforcement, MI18 are spies, The Lord Stewards are <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gmOvEwtDycs\" target=\"_blank\">civil servants</a>. You get my drift?<br /> <br /> I always liked the idea of the Chinese government hunters being economists, with a mathematical Endowment to predict the future. They make five year plans, and occasionally take care of any unpredictable elements in society. KSI-29, I always saw them as secret police, spies and secret police are similar in many regards but the differences are damn important. Now if Glamourweaver would write them, I'd find out if I'm right.<br /> <br /> <br /> Same with corporations. How many groups do you need that cut monsters up for parts? Crack open a history book or a anti-capitalist newspaper. We have Cherion cutting monsters up, but then there's the Brotherhood Prizrakov - slave-driving miners; with the Underworld instead of the Third World. The differences are big enough to make &quot;corporation&quot; almost useless as a descriptive term, and that's the way it ought to be <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So we have the vivisectionists, and the slave-drivers. Who else is out there, what other possibilities exist. How about an <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9PJNlmk5Yik\" target=\"_blank\">astral marketing firm</a>? (BTW, every now and again the question of Princess focused hunters comes up. This would be a great example of one, and no need for Hunter or Princesses to actually try to hurt each other.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-15-2014, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T14:21:13-07:00","id":170116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=169863#post169863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep thinking that there needs to be a criminal compact somewhere, an organized crime group compared to the Night Watch (Who are more street level gang members) and Ascending Ones (Who are too mystical for my tastes). Something like the mob you see in the Sopranos or Godfather, or even a yakuza branch if you want to focus on Asia. Just something that really blurs the line even more between what's right and wrong in the Vigil, since a lot of monsters use criminals like disposable pawns.</div> </div> </div> </div>you guys kill me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T16:30:34-07:00","id":170193,"title":"","content":"I have some more:<br /> <br /> - Helldivers. A Compact of explores and thrill-seekers always looking to find way enter otherwordly realms, only to turn back and share their experiences, possibly with some trophies to brag about. &quot;To go where no man has gone before&quot;. Think Edmund Hillary and Jacques Costeau, only with the Hedge and the Underworld.<br /> <br /> - A Conspiracy of (self-proclaimed?) heirs of King Solomon who bounds demons and spirits and uses their power to gather knowledge and follow God's will. Only a concept, but I have this idea to use artifacts with an imprisoned demon as an Endowment, which grant a passive bonus as long as the Hunter carries around them or, once per story or session, can be unleashed to produce powerful but dangerous effects.<br /> <br /> - A group based on the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benandanti\" target=\"_blank\">Benandanti</a><br /> <br /> - The &quot;Keepers of the Locker&quot; (I know, temp name :P) a seafaring Conspiracy that is in contact with a being that refers to itself as Davy Jones (as in, the real one). Davy Jones asks them to find beings, objects and supernatural monsters which, according to him, belong to his locker and to &quot;send them back&quot;. In exchange, he promises the Hunters treasures and mystical objects from the depths. Sure, they are only borrowed and some they he will ask them back, but still...<br /> <br /> - A Compact of thieves, and a very old one. They consider the thieves of fairy tales and myths as their illustrious predecessors, and compete with each other to steal riches and magical objects from the supernaturals. Then they throw those in the bunch or sell them because where's the fun of stealing if you use magic to cheat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 06-16-2014, 02:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T16:40:13-07:00","id":170195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=170193#post170193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have some more:<br /> <br /> - A Conspiracy of (self-proclaimed?) heirs of King Solomon who bounds demons and spirits and uses their power to gather knowledge and follow God's will. Only a concept, but I have this idea to use artifacts with an imprisoned demon as an Endowment, which grant a passive bonus as long as the Hunter carries around them or, once per story or session, can be unleashed to produce powerful but dangerous effects.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Knights of St. George are essentially this. They use goetic demons to fight witches. My headcanon for them is that they're the remnants of the Knights Templar who survived being burned as witches or disavowed by the Church; rather than be accused of witchcraft falsely, they decided that they might as well use the weapons of the Adversary against monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T16:57:30-07:00","id":170209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=170195#post170195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Knights of St. George are essentially this. They use goetic demons to fight witches. My headcanon for them is that they're the remnants of the Knights Templar who survived being burned as witches or disavowed by the Church; rather than be accused of witchcraft falsely, they decided that they might as well use the weapons of the Adversary against monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. I mean, the Gospels are named after Goetic demons (I'm going to the roots of Solomon's story and thus using the Ars Goetia is not a given, but ignoring it completely would be foolish), they are related to a real life religious group and play a dangerous game with their powers, but their background, motives, targets, Endowment and modus operandi is vastly different from what I have in mind. Not to mention the whole &quot;Faceless Angels&quot; deal.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if I can explain myself enough, mostly because it's just a concept, but I'm thinking of a group of relic wielding scholars, somewhat between the Aegis Kai Doru, the Ascending Ones and the Malleus Maleficarum, with the difference that <i>all</i> their relics can hold a conversation if the being inside it is in the right mood. They're more a &quot;Arabian Nights mystic&quot; than a &quot;Goetic witch hunter&quot; type of hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 06-15-2014, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T19:49:51-07:00","id":170349,"title":"","content":"Here are my <b>Guardians of the Vineyard</b> posted on the V:tR forum:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A vile creature poisoned the ancient and sacred vineyards of Dionysus, for She wished to claim the gardens as her own and sustain her dark children on the sweet nectar that was the wine-God's greatest gift to Humanity. Dionysus petitioned to Zeus for help against the forces of darkness. The Olympian chose to ignore his pleas, for Echidna was the daughter of Tartarus -warden of imprisoned Titans. Only when the Mother, her mate Ixion-Typhon and their blasphemous offspring assaulted Olympus and stole immortality, did the Father of Gods and Mortals take action. Ixion-Typhon was bound to a fiery wheel that would never cease spinning, and was imprisoned deep within a volcano. The Mother and her children were allowed to flee Zeus' terrible wrath, to challenge the worth of all future great warriors. We are those Heroes and Heroines. We still seek out the Dark Mother's wretched children, driving them out and reclaiming the sacred vineyards. We will cut their heads off as they feed from the sweet and holy wine of Dionysus, that is the blood of Humanity. </div> </div> </div>They mostly hunt down Vampires. Mostly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T00:28:41-07:00","id":170470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=170193#post170193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have some more:- Helldivers. A Compact of explores and thrill-seekers always looking to find way enter otherwordly realms, only to turn back and share their experiences, possibly with some trophies to brag about. &quot;To go where no man has gone before&quot;. Think Edmund Hillary and Jacques Costeau, only with the Hedge and the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div> Check my index <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T01:38:27-07:00","id":170515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes and no. I mean, the Gospels are named after Goetic demons (I'm going to the roots of Solomon's story and thus using the Ars Goetia is not a given, but ignoring it completely would be foolish), they are related to a real life religious group and play a dangerous game with their powers, but their background, motives, targets, Endowment and modus operandi is vastly different from what I have in mind. Not to mention the whole &quot;Faceless Angels&quot; deal.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if I can explain myself enough, mostly because it's just a concept, but I'm thinking of a group of relic wielding scholars, somewhat between the Aegis Kai Doru, the Ascending Ones and the Malleus Maleficarum, with the difference that <i>all</i> their relics can hold a conversation if the being inside it is in the right mood. They're more a &quot;Arabian Nights mystic&quot; than a &quot;Goetic witch hunter&quot; type of hunters. </div> </div> </div>Sounds good. Specially the option of releasing the entity. which unless the hunter had been really, really kind with it, may be the equivalent of mutual assured destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T03:04:13-07:00","id":170530,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=170470#post170470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Check my index <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose you're referring to the Soci\u00e9t\u00e9 d\u2019Had\u00e8s. I haven't read them before, so thanks for sharing.<br /> <br /> Well, yes, they cover more or less what I had in mind, but I still think there's room for another Compact of explorers, mostly because the Helldivers would not be &quot;limited&quot; (and I mean this in the most positive meaning of the word) to the Underworld, but would travel to other dimensions and unexplored places as well. Hedge, Shadow, the Astral, space or depths of the ocean...all is fair. They're essentially a gentlemen's club populated of the kind of explorers you would find in the Arthur Conand Doyle, Jules Verne or <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252525\">H. Rider. Haggard </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">stories splashed with a bit of Void Engineers from CWoD. Still, I would hate to step on the toes of the good work you did with Soci\u00e9t\u00e9, so I'll try to differentiate them some more. That said, I figure the two groups will see each other as worthy rivals indeed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=170515#post170515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds good. Specially the option of releasing the entity. which unless the hunter had been really, really kind with it, may be the equivalent of mutual assured destruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. The Endowment idea already presents a lot of interesting plot hooks like &quot;If, to release a swarm of flesh eating flies on a cult of vampires, I released a being that call himself Beelzebub from this urn, what's the deal with other urns with &quot;other&quot; Beelzebub inside? Are they different demons or pieces of a bigger entity?&quot; or &quot;What happens between the time where the demons is unleashed and when we capture it back?&quot; &quot;Why it's not <i>that </i>hard to find our missing demons, as if they want deep down to be imprisoned again?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 06-16-2014, 06:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T05:21:23-07:00","id":170584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=169863#post169863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep thinking that there needs to be a criminal compact somewhere, an organized crime group compared to the Night Watch (Who are more street level gang members) and Ascending Ones (Who are too mystical for my tastes). Something like the mob you see in the Sopranos or Godfather, or even a yakuza branch if you want to focus on Asia. Just something that really blurs the line even more between what's right and wrong in the Vigil, since a lot of monsters use criminals like disposable pawns.</div> </div> </div> </div>For some odd reason, I remember seeing a criminal compact in the Levvaithen: the Tempest project- but I can't find it anywhere. Perhaps I imagined it? 0_0<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=169863#post169863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;Keepers of the Locker&quot; (I know, temp name :P) a seafaring Conspiracy that is in contact with a being that refers to itself as Davy Jones (as in, the real one). Davy Jones asks them to find beings, objects and supernatural monsters which, according to him, belong to his locker and to &quot;send them back&quot;. In exchange, he promises the Hunters treasures and mystical objects from the depths. Sure, they are only borrowed and some they he will ask them back, but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I've also had an idea for that :P<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Queen Anne\u2019s Revenge- named after the ship of the notorious pirate Edward Thatch, they hail from the Golden Age of Piracy. Yet, as piracy fell from its grace, they found other ways to adept to the new world. By using their knowledge about buried treasures, lore gained from the &quot;heretics&quot; and connections with &quot;friends from higher places&quot;, they managed to survive to the modern world. They still see themselves as &quot;pirates&quot;, although most of them don't go on ships anymore- and some are even &quot;internet pirates&quot;. If they have Endowments, then they may be similar in nature to the AKD- but their &quot;relics&quot; work only on certain places, with more powerful the &quot;treasure&quot; more rare is the location. </div> </div> </div>maybe we should join hands and see what could turn out of it? (after I'll finish with my Oracles)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T05:41:39-07:00","id":170632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=170584#post170584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some odd reason, I remember seeing a criminal compact in the Levvaithen: the Tempest project- but I can't find it anywhere. Perhaps I imagined it? 0_0</div> </div> </div> </div>It's here: <a href=\"http://wiki.rpg.net/index.php/LeviathanTempest:LlenlleawchDumpingGround\" target=\"_blank\">http://wiki.rpg.net/index.php/Leviat...hDumpingGround</a><br /> <br /> <br /> We discussed it on the development forums, but there was no consensus to include them. They ended up on the wiki anyway, and left a while later. Hence your memory. If your curious the reason was that they seemed too small, too local. Leviathan is a game with a, pardon the pun, large scale. Marduk is a lot smaller than most people suspect, but it's still on all seven continents, seven seas, and even outer space. The Irrational Economic Actors task force are part of the enormous European Union. The Season Letters are small, and at least get in by being Lovecraft investigator types. The Tucker Street boys just didn't quite fit.<br /> <br /> If I were to do criminals for Leviathan, I'd probably talk about the Mafia, or a similarly large non-Hunter organization, mention how they might fight Leviathans, and then back them up with a Compact who are explicitly professional Leviathan hunters (perhaps originating from Japanese whalers, because Japan &lt;--&gt; Kaiju) that any of the syndicates might commission.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T06:35:53-07:00","id":170670,"title":"","content":"<b>The Last Wilderness Rangers</b><br /> <br /> The Last Wilderness Rangers are an American scout group known to be a strange mix of liberal environmentalists and old-style huntsmen - the founder was a man who believed, deeply, in all the old legends of how to woods and wilderness had power, and how that power could be very dangerous. The Rangers are a growing sight in small towns, due to their very open recruitment drives - boy, girls, gay, troubled, clean-cut, all are welcome to join the Rangers. The reason for this is twofold; firstly, the group does believe that their lessons and instructions (primarily focused on living cleanly within nature and respecting the myths and legends of diverse cultures) do in fact help young people. The second reason is that with a wider net comes greater possibility of finding people who have the right stuff to be inducted in the Inner Circle.<br /> <br /> The Inner Circle are a secret group within the Wilderness Rangers who have both completed all the levels of Rangerhood (Cat, Fox, Deer, Hawk, Wolf) and have shown to current Inner Circle members that the the right mentality to join the Vigil. The idea is that the years within the Rangers would help foster a strong loyalty to the group and allow older, more experienced members to help guide the prospects on the right path to be an efficient an productive Hunter.<br /> <br /> The Rangers see their Vigil as the protection of the next generation (in a 'teach a man to fish' sort of way) and the watchers of the wilderness. they hunt down the strange creatures that roam the hills and valleys of the Americas, the small towns that abut the deep, dark woods. They listen to the old legends and stories, spreading them around the camp fires so that they are not forgotten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T07:34:55-07:00","id":170722,"title":"","content":"I once had an idea for a Hunter conspiracy who fancy themselves heirs to monster-slaying heroes like Hercules, Beowulf or Siegfried. They would be obsessed over self-perfection and denial of weakness; probably have some racist and eugenic elements too. I'm not sure what their Endowment would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T09:07:41-07:00","id":170795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=170632#post170632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's here: <a href=\"http://wiki.rpg.net/index.php/LeviathanTempest:LlenlleawchDumpingGround\" target=\"_blank\">http://wiki.rpg.net/index.php/Leviat...hDumpingGround</a><br /> <br /> <br /> We discussed it on the development forums, but there was no consensus to include them. They ended up on the wiki anyway, and left a while later. Hence your memory. If your curious the reason was that they seemed too small, too local. Leviathan is a game with a, pardon the pun, large scale. Marduk is a lot smaller than most people suspect, but it's still on all seven continents, seven seas, and even outer space. The Irrational Economic Actors task force are part of the enormous European Union. The Season Letters are small, and at least get in by being Lovecraft investigator types. The Tucker Street boys just didn't quite fit.<br /> <br /> If I were to do criminals for Leviathan, I'd probably talk about the Mafia, or a similarly large non-Hunter organization, mention how they might fight Leviathans, and then back them up with a Compact who are explicitly professional Leviathan hunters (perhaps originating from Japanese whalers, because Japan &lt;--&gt; Kaiju) that any of the syndicates might commission.</div> </div> </div> </div>thank you for that. I've almost thought I was hallucinating thing :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T03:42:03-07:00","id":173922,"title":"","content":"so, I've lately looked on all my previous organization ideas, and I've found two old ones which I'm still interest in writing one day. Here are their temp names:<br /> <br /> Memory Collectors- a compact of art collectors and historians, who see the whole Underworld as a huge library which contains all knowledge which ever existed. They collect both memorabilia (for they contain power for their very importance in human history) and Fetters (which hold the ghosts of the dead and allows them ton gain their knowledge). They are extremely interested in finding the ghosts and memorabilia of important people, like artists, politicians and similar famous people, and while the generally wait for them to die and hope that they would leave a ghost behind, some take a more.. active approach.<br /> <br /> Solifacti- another Slashing Conspiracy, they originate from the Mendeleev. They are alchemists which sought after eternal life and the Philosopher Stone, until they came to the conclusion that the mythical substance was no other than the human soul- and so, they must harvest it. They use human organs in their alchemical formulas, and they use it in order to improve themselves, change lead to gold, create energy out of matter and more- yet they still didn't found the organ which contains the &quot;soul&quot;- and they are sure that when they would find it, they will gain immortality. Their Endowments may be similar to Elixirs, just with a dark twist.<br /> <br /> and a two new ideas:<br /> <br /> Emerald Gardeners- a conspiracy which seeks to gain control over the Hedge, for they see it as a potential way to create wondrous and terrible things. For them, it is a tool to be used by humanity, and they while it has a corrupting effect on the human soul, they are still willing to place a &quot;seed from the Hedge&quot; in their heart in order to be able to conjure its vines and bushes for their help. While it allows them to conjure weird things and create all kinds of weird materials, each dot in their Endowments breaks their mind, slowly but surely.<br /> <br /> Wu Keng- yes, I know, but just listen. They are going to be &quot;demon hunters&quot;, both lesser and greater, although they don't actually hunt the demons. They trick them. The are a modern creation based on an older version of the group, which have used the traditional cross dressing tradition in order to trick demons and null their pacts. Each member of the organization has an &quot;alternative Cover&quot; which is activate once they are dressed as the opposite gender, and any kind of supernatural effect which targets a specific individual (especially demonic pacts) target the alternative identity and their true identity as two different individuals. That way, they can make a pact with a demons, but when the demons wish to get his side in the deal they simply destroy the &quot;Cover&quot;. While it also destroys what they gained from the pact, they can &quot;cash&quot; the effect in order to get Dread Powers.<br /> <br /> any thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T10:38:20-07:00","id":174270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=173922#post173922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wu Keng</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm interested in these guys, girls and variations thereupon.<br /> <br /> Is their motive defending humanity, or just getting rich?<br /> <br /> If it's defending humanity, I'd skip out the infernal demons or their hunterised equivalents. There's just nothing good that can come of interacting with them. If it's the second I'd either throw in faeries and any other pact making monsters; unless said monsters have an ability to bypass the cover with their pacts.<br /> <br /> Actually, thinking about it. Both Fae and Unchained basically serve as intermediarais with supernatural mechanisms while Infernals and Spirits have to provide their end of the bargain by hand. Drawing a distinction between those two types might be useful for justifying why they focus on some monsters and not others.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T11:00:45-07:00","id":174284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=174270#post174270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm interested in these guys, girls and variations thereupon.<br /> <br /> Is their motive defending humanity, or just getting rich?<br /> <br /> If it's defending humanity, I'd skip out the infernal demons or their hunterised equivalents. There's just nothing good that can come of interacting with them. If it's the second I'd either throw in faeries and any other pact making monsters; unless said monsters have an ability to bypass the cover with their pacts.<br /> <br /> Actually, thinking about it. Both Fae and Unchained basically serve as intermediarais with supernatural mechanisms while Infernals and Spirits have to provide their end of the bargain by hand. Drawing a distinction between those two types might be useful for justifying why they focus on some monsters and not others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm kind of leaning toward the second option, simply because I can't see them as the altruistic type of organization. They are tricksters and cheaters who make a pact with a demon, give him some &quot;part of their life&quot; until suddenly the demon discover he got nothing while the hunter is laughing all the way to the bank. Note, it is not that they can't be the defenders of humanity. It is just that I can't see it that way while they are still in a &quot;pitch&quot; phase.<br /> <br /> Also, yeah, I think they should also make pacts with the faeries in their like- this is why I said their Endowments makes them into someone else entirely as far as supernatural powers are concerned. You also bring up a good point with the distinction between ephemeral and physical &quot;pact making&quot; beings. I think that because of their Endowment, they'll focus on the Greater Demons and the Gentry- but it doesn't stop them from messing around with other beings, believing with the power of their &quot;Cover&quot; to protect them from their wrath in the same way Demons hide from Angels.<br /> <br /> Is it a good direction?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T11:17:46-07:00","id":174314,"title":"","content":"Seems like a good direction; apart from your insistence of using the Greater/Lesser demon terminology which distances you from the distinction between Infernal &amp; Unchained; and given this is about pacts, you want to make full use of the fact both have a unique pact style.<br /> <br /> Though I am starting to wonder if they might work better as a Merit; rather than being an organisation it's a technique that's used by a verity of hunters, witches* and miscellaneous. Most of whom don't know of any others.<br /> <br /> <br /> *The kind who don't have a major template.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T11:39:57-07:00","id":174378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=174314#post174314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like a good direction; apart from your insistence of using the Greater/Lesser demon terminology which distances you from the distinction between Infernal &amp; Unchained; and given this is about pacts, you want to make full use of the fact both have a unique pact style.<br /> <br /> Though I am starting to wonder if they might work better as a Merit; rather than being an organisation it's a technique that's used by a verity of hunters, witches* and miscellaneous. Most of whom don't know of any others.<br /> <br /> <br /> *The kind who don't have a major template.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Endowments are, by their very essence, Merits. A Conspiracy is simply a group of people who specialize in certain types of such Merits. Sure, there are exceptions (like the Lucifuge), to which Endowments are tied to the very nature of the organization, but one could use the equivalents of some Endowments by having a certain Merit (at least, that is my Hunter worldview. Feel free to disagree). In short, the Wu Keng would simply be an organization focused on the technique, while there may be other groups or individuals who may discover the secret by themselves. I may even write a sidebar about that if I'll make them into a full writeup. Also, remember that in the current phase, they are supposed to &quot;cash&quot; the benefits given them by their Pacts into Dread Powers once they destroy the false identity, which kinda makes them less a special Merit on more a Conspiracy.<br /> <br /> Also, the reason I use &quot;Greater&quot; and &quot;Lesser&quot; is because that was the terminology given by Mortal Remains, but I think about them as Infernal and Unchained, so this is covered :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T11:53:57-07:00","id":174403,"title":"","content":"Well it's more that, I find the Endowment to be an awesome idea but the idea of a group that specialises in it doesn't interest me that much.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for greater and lesser. Using those terms implies to me that you're using the Mortal Remains rules that blend the two; no big deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T11:57:37-07:00","id":174407,"title":"","content":"well, once I'll write them, feel free to scavenge what you want. It is simply that for some reason, I really like the CWoD Wu Keng's concept, and I think it could work as a nice Conspiracy :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T12:35:32-07:00","id":174445,"title":"","content":"Get writing *whip*<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T09:51:01-07:00","id":175314,"title":"","content":"It really seems like the books have managed to cover most of the bases. Everything I think of is some variant of 'like that existing group, but with this instead of that.' But maybe I'm too close, being a fan of the game line.<br /> <br /> So, in the vein of Ashwood Abbey, but with money instead of thrills, how about 'The House.' Essentially an underground gambling syndicate that has operatives that act to poke the bears, so to speak, provoking monsters into act, and betting on how they'll react. Obviously among the many problems with this is the big one that implies that they already know about supernaturals and how they act, which already makes them more informed than most hunter compacts. But, say, a bunch of wealthy folks (and some not-so-wealthy but connected to the underground necessary to make the operation worked) started having some death sports. Bum fights to the death. And one day things got weird when Something Happened. Maybe a demon went loud or a werewolf death raged or a promethean let loose. Either way, a group of insiders formed, realizing they could get wealthy folks into it. Sure, some folks could be fulfilled by a contract with the Bear Lodge or the Ashwood Abbey, but who wants to get their hands dirty when they could watch others do so from the comfort of their home and an internet connection?<br /> <br /> While there'd be the folks who do the behind the scenes work (getting investors involved, scouting out staging grounds, maintaining the servers) the hard but well-rewarded work would be done by the folks who scout out locations and 'political' situations so they could send in the grunts, who do the real hard work, doing things like luring pure into forsaken territories, angels to demons, pointing hunters towards vampire havens and, rarely, just out and out kidnapping to drop things into a makeshift arena.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T13:57:14-07:00","id":180049,"title":"","content":"I myself have been toying with the idea of a Compact that's like the Ashwood Abbey, if they were motivated by Nihilism, or similar, in a way, rather than pleasure. Their lives have in some way been demolished to the point where they don't care anymore. The only ways they feel their lives can matter anymore is by killing those that destroyed their lives to begin with, or if this group possibly forms in relation to the God Machine, damaging its schemes. Another element would be them somehow trying to draw attention to themselves, almost like the Hunter equivalent of... Internet trolls. The last idea probably wouldn't work, but just a thought. <br /> <br /> The over all thing suffers from that... well, its problematic. Hitting rock bottom isn't enough, in of itself, to form a Compact, so I need to work on something else related to that.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T19:23:54-07:00","id":180274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=173922#post173922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so, I've lately looked on all my previous organization ideas, and I've found two old ones which I'm still interest in writing one day. Here are their temp names:<br /> <br /> Memory Collectors- a compact of art collectors and historians, who see the whole Underworld as a huge library which contains all knowledge which ever existed. They collect both memorabilia (for they contain power for their very importance in human history) and Fetters (which hold the ghosts of the dead and allows them ton gain their knowledge). They are extremely interested in finding the ghosts and memorabilia of important people, like artists, politicians and similar famous people, and while the generally wait for them to die and hope that they would leave a ghost behind, some take a more.. active approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't the latter group have a... umm, rather hard time? It isn't exactly easy to assassinate politicians and the like after all.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> More importantly though, isn't this kind of stepping on the toes of the Relic group? Both are obsessed with important objects, and I'm sure relics left by important dead people would be in that area. Yes, they have a different justification but... well, I'd just hope they did something at least somewhat different with the objects. For that matter, killing important people also overlaps a bit with the Hunt Club, and I know that being similar to another Hunter group is hardly bad in of itself, but still... I don't know. I feel like this one needs another component to become more fully fleshed out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Solifacti- another Slashing Conspiracy, they originate from the Mendeleev. They are alchemists which sought after eternal life and the Philosopher Stone, until they came to the conclusion that the mythical substance was no other than the human soul- and so, they must harvest it. They use human organs in their alchemical formulas, and they use it in order to improve themselves, change lead to gold, create energy out of matter and more- yet they still didn't found the organ which contains the &quot;soul&quot;- and they are sure that when they would find it, they will gain immortality. Their Endowments may be similar to Elixirs, just with a dark twist. </div> </div> </div>Now this is awesome, seeing as, to my knowledge, we only have one other Slasher centric Conspiracy, and only one official Slasher group, itself a Compact. That, and the idea of a group devoted to finding certain organs has plenty of cool ideas with it. Question is, do they perhaps consider monsters for their organs as well? Something to consider within their ideology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Emerald Gardeners- a conspiracy which seeks to gain control over the Hedge, for they see it as a potential way to create wondrous and terrible things. For them, it is a tool to be used by humanity, and they while it has a corrupting effect on the human soul, they are still willing to place a &quot;seed from the Hedge&quot; in their heart in order to be able to conjure its vines and bushes for their help. While it allows them to conjure weird things and create all kinds of weird materials, each dot in their Endowments breaks their mind, slowly but surely. </div> </div> </div>Umm, wouldn't the Gentry, and for that matter, Hedge Goblins eventually demolish them? Somehow, I don't think just screwing around in the Hedge is really the best idea for Mortals, even if they addimately have some magical tricks, and changing the Hedge, which is this seems to imply, doesn't sound like something the setting will really allow for most of the time. Just food for thought.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wu Keng- yes, I know, but just listen. They are going to be &quot;demon hunters&quot;, both lesser and greater, although they don't actually hunt the demons. They trick them. The are a modern creation based on an older version of the group, which have used the traditional cross dressing tradition in order to trick demons and null their pacts. Each member of the organization has an &quot;alternative Cover&quot; which is activate once they are dressed as the opposite gender, and any kind of supernatural effect which targets a specific individual (especially demonic pacts) target the alternative identity and their true identity as two different individuals. That way, they can make a pact with a demons, but when the demons wish to get his side in the deal they simply destroy the &quot;Cover&quot;. While it also destroys what they gained from the pact, they can &quot;cash&quot; the effect in order to get Dread Powers. </div> </div> </div>This one I actually like the idea of, partially because I think trickster style Hunters are a bit underutilized right now. For another, this is a socially centric group I'd imagine, because they'd need to know how to, &quot;pretend,&quot; to be the alternate cover, all things considered, and those are quite rare from what I understand. And finally, their core endowment does sound quite interesting, to say the least.<br /> <br /> Hope all this fueled more creativity from you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T13:14:22-07:00","id":181184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=175314#post175314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really seems like the books have managed to cover most of the bases. Everything I think of is some variant of 'like that existing group, but with this instead of that.' But maybe I'm too close, being a fan of the game line.<br /> <br /> So, in the vein of Ashwood Abbey, but with money instead of thrills, how about 'The House.' Essentially an underground gambling syndicate that has operatives that act to poke the bears, so to speak, provoking monsters into act, and betting on how they'll react. Obviously among the many problems with this is the big one that implies that they already know about supernaturals and how they act, which already makes them more informed than most hunter compacts. But, say, a bunch of wealthy folks (and some not-so-wealthy but connected to the underground necessary to make the operation worked) started having some death sports. Bum fights to the death. And one day things got weird when Something Happened. Maybe a demon went loud or a werewolf death raged or a promethean let loose. Either way, a group of insiders formed, realizing they could get wealthy folks into it. Sure, some folks could be fulfilled by a contract with the Bear Lodge or the Ashwood Abbey, but who wants to get their hands dirty when they could watch others do so from the comfort of their home and an internet connection?<br /> <br /> While there'd be the folks who do the behind the scenes work (getting investors involved, scouting out staging grounds, maintaining the servers) the hard but well-rewarded work would be done by the folks who scout out locations and 'political' situations so they could send in the grunts, who do the real hard work, doing things like luring pure into forsaken territories, angels to demons, pointing hunters towards vampire havens and, rarely, just out and out kidnapping to drop things into a makeshift arena.</div> </div> </div> </div>The major problem with this one is the amount of knowledge required on the part of the organization itself is... pretty high. They'd need to know where to find Werewolves, which I doubt is a simple affair, and they also have to set up cameras or something so that the following fight can be watched. Except, depending on where it is, unless they somehow drag the monsters back to a pit of some kind, they'll find the angle will probably suck. And that would matter for the patrons I'd imagine. <br /> Vampires, by the way, would spoil things because they just show up as fuzzy images, which would probably make the recording a lot less, &quot;fun,&quot; to say the least.<br /> <br /> Sorry. They just come as the Ashwood Abbey, if they were a lot lazier yet paradoxically more knowledgable. Hope this helps you come up something else though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T13:43:43-07:00","id":181205,"title":"","content":"<b>Federal Faiths Mutual:</b> The <i>only</i> insurance company that fully covers Acts of God (and Werewolf, and Vampire, and Promethean...) They insure several other Compacts; ideally, they'll get that agreement signed with Cheiron any day now. They are a <i>respectable</i> company, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T14:30:50-07:00","id":181242,"title":"","content":"One of these days, I should write up that group from Geist that venerates Sin-Eaters as gods and hopes to become them. Maybe lump them in with the folks from Changeling who want to become changelings and have a whole &quot;supernatural groupie&quot; compact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T14:44:05-07:00","id":181261,"title":"","content":"Some concepts work best when they're not organised into groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T09:05:27-07:00","id":185581,"title":"","content":"I have two rough-sketches of ideas:<br /> <br /> The first is the Friends of the Deceased, a Compact whose members believe in the sanctity of the afterlife. They know ghosts exist, and, unlike many denizens of the World of Darkness, believe them to be actual continuations of the people they were in life. They take desecration of the dead <i>very</i> seriously, and depending on where you are, any given cell might range from a particularly quirky local historical society, to a spectral ALF. Ghosts, whatever the truth may be, like them, since the Friends keep them in supply of Essence and lucidity. As far as Hunter activities go, they're primarily a social threat, taking advantage of the emotional ties people have to the dead. Wealthy members might arrange funerals for those whose families can't afford them, while others might show up graveside with a hip flask and a shoulder to cry on. Their primary targets are anyone who abuses the dead--necromancers, ectophages, bokor, etc.<br /> <br /> The second is a Conspiracy I was thinking of today, though they're a bit muddled at the moment. It started with the idea of an Endowment in the form of a &quot;pet&quot; Pandoran--a horrific twist on the &quot;bonded companion&quot; trope. The Conspiracy has some sort of connection to the Divine Fire; maybe alchemists of some sort, maybe religious scientists, maybe wannabe Demiurges (one might consider all three of these to be the same thing, of course). They provide members with a small object filled with Vitriol, which is alchemically-attuned to a specific Pandoran. The hunter can use the device to awaken the monster, though naturally it's difficult to control and will viciously attack any source of Pyros it comes across.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T07:39:05-07:00","id":191389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=185581#post185581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have two rough-sketches of ideas:<br /> <br /> The first is the Friends of the Deceased, a Compact whose members believe in the sanctity of the afterlife. They know ghosts exist, and, unlike many denizens of the World of Darkness, believe them to be actual continuations of the people they were in life. They take desecration of the dead <i>very</i> seriously, and depending on where you are, any given cell might range from a particularly quirky local historical society, to a spectral ALF. Ghosts, whatever the truth may be, like them, since the Friends keep them in supply of Essence and lucidity. As far as Hunter activities go, they're primarily a social threat, taking advantage of the emotional ties people have to the dead. Wealthy members might arrange funerals for those whose families can't afford them, while others might show up graveside with a hip flask and a shoulder to cry on. Their primary targets are anyone who abuses the dead--necromancers, ectophages, bokor, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I steal this one and flesh it out? The words &quot;Speaker for the Dead&quot; drifted through my head and I felt plotty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T09:29:13-07:00","id":191465,"title":"","content":"Go for it! I'm glad you liked my idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T10:00:16-07:00","id":191492,"title":"","content":"I might take it a different flavor than you did, perhaps finding a culture to play off of. Jewish funerary rites, mmm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T04:08:59-07:00","id":193377,"title":"","content":"Off the top of my head (and because I've been reading some Mythos related material), I've got a few ideas for Compacts:<br /> <br /> 1) The Innsmouth Collective: An off shoot of the Marsh Family of Old Innsmouth who learned of curse they bear and are now trying to find ways to stop it. They hunt in order to interrogate and dissect monsters to better understand their own condition. Unlike their country kin, they make it a point to be sophisticated and live as far as they can from the sea and it's Call. Most are very well learned as well.<br /> <br /> 2) The Dunwich Militia: After their town was ravaged by a Horror, the men of Dunwich have taken it upon themselves to never be unprepared for creatures like the Whateley Brothers again! The Militia began it's training under Dr. Armitage and, while the Good Doctor had to return to his school, the men kept on with their studies. Using books Armitage left behind as well as correspondence with the Miskatonic Teaching Staff, the Militia has kept both their town and the surrounding area safe from unknowable creatures from beyond time and space. They also spit a mean hog.<br /> <br /> 3) The Miskatonic Teaching Staff: Arkham's famed center for higher learning has always attracted a specfic element to it's hallowed halls. It is only through the continued vigilance of it's world renown Teaching Staff that the world has not fallen into utter ruin! Seriously, all it takes is the wrong freshman making off with a book from the restricted section for the Dead to Rise and the Sun to be blotted out from the Sky. The leader of the Staff, the Dean (not the head of the school however), is very good at sending the right professor for the right job. I thought about making them a Conspiracy that had access to Dark Magics that cost them their Sanity. The &quot;Retired Staff&quot; are those teachers that now reside in Arkham Sanitarium. They may not have &quot;Tenure&quot; anymore, but they still have knowledge to share!<br /> <br /> Anyway, just some thoughts. Not really fleshed out yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1101-blindst","name":"blindST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T07:04:51-07:00","id":193535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=191492#post191492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might take it a different flavor than you did, perhaps finding a culture to play off of. Jewish funerary rites, mmm.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's cool. I'm not sure how helpful you'll find it, but <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rMBZZwgmhCgIsTIvFrRtZts_y4Mhsnt9Pbuzf7rWbIU/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">here are my notes on the Compact</a>. Even though they're written with a neo-Victorian aesthetic in mind, you might find something to salvage in them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T07:28:08-07:00","id":193547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=193535#post193535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's cool. I'm not sure how helpful you'll find it, but <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rMBZZwgmhCgIsTIvFrRtZts_y4Mhsnt9Pbuzf7rWbIU/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">here are my notes on the Compact</a>. Even though they're written with a neo-Victorian aesthetic in mind, you might find something to salvage in them.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lot there that I really like, in the tone. Take all of that and fold in a bissel of the mitzvah of comforting the bereaved...though what you have's a pretty complete thought in itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T15:01:55-07:00","id":193999,"title":"","content":"I wanted to design something more oriental for Hunter: The Vigil, but all I come up with is stuff about ninjas. Actually, I got really inspired from reading about a video game conspiracy (Secret World) simply called &quot;Dragon&quot; that focuses around the &quot;Art of Chaos.&quot; Tell me what you think. <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>The Dragon Lotus</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><i>Masters of the Nameless Path</i></div> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <i>&quot;Change requires chaos, and chaos is ours to orchestrate.&quot;</i></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">A controlled society is a sick society, especially one secretly ruled by the supernatural. The Order of the Dragon Lotus wishes to keep all things in harmony by allowing the natural flow of Chaos to balance the stagnation of corrupted Order. The teachings of the Dragon Lotus were first taught by a man simply called the Green Monk, who uncovered a rare flower atop the peaks of a mountain. Where this mountain was changes with each telling, but has always been believed to be within Asia. It is said that, for days and nights, the Green Monk contemplated the flower, and how its petals moved with the currents of the wind. From this did he scribe the sacred teachings of the Dragon Lotus, which taught of strange magics that would bring about the greatest change onto a world stagnant and dying. However, creatures from the shadows detested the Green Monk's work, seeing their bases of power crumbling into oblivion as the mortal gained followers both noble and commoner. Quickly, they attempted to take his life and end his meddling, but the stone had been cast, and ripples would grow.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">For centuries, the conspiracy has existed, rising and falling as their needs are met. Their strategies are incomprehensible to any and all outsiders looking for a pattern. To the dragons, however, there is no pattern, only a chain of events set off by a single action. Every cell acts separate from the other, yet all are united in their cause to save humanity from within and out. Whether by sponsoring a secret dojo, blowing up a vampire's haven, or simply warning a witch of another hunter, all is ethical so long as it brings chaos to heal a paralyzed world.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Factions</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Dragon Disciples are made up of those most intent on studying the teachings of the Green Monk. Cautiously, they observe chaos from a distance and seek to learn from what later transpires from it. This makes them appear less involved with the world, but their knowledge has granted them a rather uncanny foresight in the actions of both human and supernatural creature. Enough, at least, to stay one step ahead of them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Emerald Flame is the &quot;teeth of the dragon&quot;. Though not comprised of just anarchists and vigilantes, this faction encourages active attempts to harass the supernatural, especially ones with great control over the status-quo. Like fire, they burn away the disease that plagues humanity, and yet, like the emerald, they do so to heal and bring natural harmony to all.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Unified believe that the order should keep better connection with its various cells. Too many times have fellow dragons crossed each other by accident and brought about their deaths due to lack of coordination. However, critics of the faction see this a violation of the Green Monk's teachings. They argue that even those who master chaos must still accept that they are not immune to it, lest they abuse their power and become like the monsters they fight.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>New Endowment: Dragon Sutra</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Through the lessons taught by the Green Monk, his disciples learned to guide the ebb and flow of chaos to aid them in their cause. These teachings, called dragon sutras, are taught to agents of the order to utilize in the eternal shadow war. </span></span><br /> <br /> <i>Changing Face</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Similar to Hens\u014djutsu, the art of disguise and impersonation, the sutra of Changing Face teaches that even the truth is subjective to chaos when the mind is unprepared. Channeling the force of chaos into her face, a dragon agent can alter its texture and shape for a number of hours equal to successes rolled.</span></span><br /> <br /> <i>Seed of Discord</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">An advanced sutra based on subtlety and deception, the agent plants a suggestion in the mind of his target through a simple phrase or gesture. This suggestion is one of rebellion that, as time goes by, becomes harder and harder to ignore. Once acted upon, however, the target is released of the urge completely (unless it was already there to begin with).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Cost: 1 Willpower Point</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Action: Instant; contested.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Dice Pool: Manipulation + Dragon Sutra vs Composure. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Roll Results</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Dramatic Failure: As per failure, save the target cannot be affected by the sutra for another twenty-four hours. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Failure: Nothing happens.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Success: The target becomes compelled to act against what they perceive as oppressive. The target is allowed to resist the compulsion with a Resolve + Composure check each hour, but gain a -1 to that check per hour they resist until either knocked unconscious or the effect is dispelled supernaturally. The caster has no control over the sutra once it has been cast, nor can he dispel the effects whenever he pleases.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Exceptional Success: As per success, save the agent can dictate what the target rebels against.</span></span><br /> <br /> <i>Yanwei Fengbao</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Yanwei, or &quot;swallowtail,&quot; is a butterfly native to the provinces of China. Based on the concept of the Butterfly Effect (or perhaps the other way around), the dragon agent can channel the forces of chaos into a single action, which will cause a domino effect to take place. Depending on the number of successes rolled, this will either bring about good or ill fortune in the near future.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T17:15:50-07:00","id":194125,"title":"","content":"I'm probably gonna do some more <i>Delta Green </i>conversions: while Majestic-12 doesn't work without aliens, groups like GRU SV-8 (DG's Russian equivalent, desperately underfunded and understaffed), PISCES (the United Kingdom's anti-supernatural group, bolstered by psychics but compromised by alien insects), The Fate (sorcerers-for-hire that run in criminal circles and rule New York's underground), and the Karotechia (an antagonist group; the far-flung remnants of Nazi Germany's occult weapons program, now nearly destroyed and consisting largely of modern hate groups with no knowledge of magic).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T03:04:29-07:00","id":198769,"title":"","content":"I don't know M-12 could believe that specific types of supernatural creatures are actually aliens. Changelings could are already abduction victims, Demons are the former agents of an alien intelligence, Mages are people with alien blood in their families that allow them to do &quot;Magic&quot;, etc. I find, when it comes to Hunter, it's all in how you see the Monsters you come across.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1101-blindst","name":"blindST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T02:28:14-07:00","id":202770,"title":"","content":"I LOVE the Wu-Keng idea! Federal Faiths Mutual is also amusing to me, but would likely work better as NPCs than as PCs (unless maybe the PCs were insurance fraud investigators, and had to prove that the damages were insurable).<br /> <br /> I have two ideas that have been drifting through my head lately:<br /> <br /> The first don't have a name- not even a secret name or a working name. Maybe TF:V call them Unsponsored Agents (Type 4). Maybe the Lucifuge call them The Evangelicized. Let's go with that. Whatever they are called, they are individuals who developed an ability similar to the Imbued from H:tR, only the messages are even more vague and show up inside their heads instead of in the world around them. When they're near certain species of monsters (which vary from a single WoD gameline species to all species including other Evangelicized), or the creations of those species (areas of Paradox, Wyrd locations and items), they get a very, very strong feeling, almost like a conscience whispering to them, that this is a wrongness and they should get to the root of it. The monsters themselves cause the conscience to SCREAM OUT &quot;It's wrong! It's evil! Self-defend it to death!&quot; The vast majority of these Hunters get put away in psychiatric prisons for a VERY long time. A lucky (or perhaps unlucky) few manage to survive multiple encounters on their own or join a Tier 1 Conspiracy. The rarest pinnacle are brought into (or captured by) a Tier 2 or 3 Conspiracy. The Evangelicized don't get outward Imbuements. Instead, each Imbuement gives them Hunches related to the hunt. For instance, a player could spend points on I Know Your Weak Point: One point gives the hunter a slight knack for telling which traditional weaknesses a monster has through their research (Fae are weak against Cold iron, kidnapped children probably aren't), three points gives that for more specific monster lines that they are able to research (Nosferatu vs. Daeva vs. Gangrel) and a vague idea of what individual monsters' weaknesses are from looking at them, and five points basically outright tells the Hunter one or two major weaknesses that it has and one traditional weakness that it DOESN'T have. The player could also take You Can Run..., which allows the character to, say, spend a point of Willpower a certain number of times per scene to get a hint of where to go next (basically a merit that gives the character out-of-character knowledge). It's up to the DM whether these are psychic abilities, or a quashmallim, or anything else they can think of. DM is also encouraged to forbid certain merits like You Can Run... that give the character impossible knowledge, be it for game balance or to reinforce the possibility that the characters are just criminally insane and happen to have good gut instincts when it comes to hunting down monsters (a la that breed of Hannibal Lecter-esque Slasher).<br /> <br /> The other are the Sect of Returning Light (I'm sure I can come up with a better name, but I kind of like the SRL-Serial puns that can be made). They're Lucifuge whose ancestors split off from the group, or who weren't born into the Lucifuge, and were picked up by a cult who believe that they're the key to allowing demons to return to grace. Different from the Reconciliation in that they are working to return ALL their ancestral Fallen to grace, and not just Lucifer, and returning them to God's arms is a goal in and of itself (not a step in the process of destroying Hell and preventing anyone from ever being damned). The Fallen-blooded of their many splinter factions far outnumber the official 666 Lucifuge, and possibly the entire Lucifuge organization, but they rarely work together and not even the most populous branches combined have anywhere near 600 Fallen-blooded members. As could be expected, they don't have the genealogical information (or genealogical <i>propaganda</i>) that the Lucifuge use. They can summon and contain creatures of the Inferno, but unless they have the sect-specific Infernal Virus ritual that turns the creatures into mindless voodoo zombies that do nothing BUT work-to-rule, the SRLs can't control them. The truth behind the matter is that their ancestors, as Unchained, don't WANT to be allowed back into the God-Machine's grace, and the climax of a SRL character's story involves either A: unwittingly sending their ancestor back into slavery or B: discovering that they must give up either the spirit of their lifelong goal (&quot;grant my ancestor peace&quot;) or the letter of their lifelong goal (&quot;return my ancestor to their place with God&quot;).<br /> <br /> Edit: P.S.: I always liked the idea of Hunters who believe the monsters are different type of some other thing.<br /> Fairy-Hunters: Changelings? Changelings! Demons? Fae with fire and speech powers! Prometheans? Fetches and reanimated bodies! Werewolves? The True Fae equivalent of Beast changelings!<br /> Fox Mulders: Changelings? Abductees! The true fae? Aliens from another dimension! Demons? Aliens from a fiery planet on whose technology all Terran computers are based! Mummies? Goa'uld technology!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1963,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1963-jet73l","user":"JET73L","date":". 07-20-2014, 05:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1963-jet73l","name":"JET73L","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T21:17:21-07:00","id":205632,"title":"","content":"I've been making a group of Magical Girls who are Changeling focused. The Starlight Sisterhood.<br /> <br /> They were young women who were kidnapped by Fae but saved before becoming Changelings. Essentially they're Faetouched. They've got a powerful &quot;Patron&quot; (Who's an Exiled True Fae who has taken on the role of guiding young women to become magical girls... and also to murder the crap out of other True Fae because screw those guys) and can gain powers by making deals with the creatures of the &quot;Dark Forest&quot;, which is what they refer to the Hedge as. They're made for going after True Fae, Fetches, and the occasional Changeling. As a Conspiracy, they've actually got a small brand of cartoons and comic books and action figures marketed towards girls (and of course weirdly obsessed adult men), encouraging them to be princesses and heroes. Instilling the group's ideals into them in case one day they get snatched out of their beds by the Fae, and find themselves rescued by older girls, each one strong and determined there in the Dark Forest.<br /> <br /> Their powers are &quot;Pactio&quot; (for the moment), and represent bargains and deals that they've made with the entities of the Dark Forest (hobgoblins, changelings, the occasional Exile). I'm thinking they should have Drawbacks and catches. And they might even have heavy prices that they have to pay to learn the Pact, similar to how Goblin Markets work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 07-23-2014, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T14:54:36-07:00","id":210590,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">Since I'm apparently a Lovecraft-obsessed idiot, I've been reading <i>Trail of Cthulhu</i> rather obsessively, and found that the example campaign frames make sound Compact ideas. While Project Covenant is Delta Green in all but name (and as such, already written up by me) and the Armitage Inquiry is basically the Loyalists of Thule with a different backstory (occult scholars with a focus on keeping their knowledge secret from the public), the Book-Hounds of London occupy a niche that hasn't really been hit on in <i>Hunter</i>. While the Night Watch has the criminal aspect down and a number of groups (Cheiron chief among them) take to the Vigil for selfish/profitable reasons, that combination is unique. Before I throw an afternoon's work into this conversion, could I see what you guys think of the pitch?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#444444\">Buyers exist for damn near anything on the planet; the Book-Hounds know this, and cater to those with esoteric tastes. They track down and sell Mythos texts, relics, and works of art to sell to the highest bidders in the United Kingdom. Equally comprised of antiquarians, forgers, and common thugs, the average Book-Hound is a ruthless occult criminal who has seen and done things that would break weaker men.</span> </div> </div> </div></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T22:27:27-07:00","id":210876,"title":"","content":"To me the appeal of hunter comes from the image of being hopelessly out-numbered, from the glorious, if vain struggle of it all. Early in the thread someone mentioned doing a folklore monster-slayer throw-back themed group, so I'm going to kick that around and see what I can churn out. I picture them being sort of the shining, epic version of the Lucifuge.<br /> <br /> The tentative name of the group is <b>The Descendants</b><b>,</b> because it's less conspicuous sounding than the <b>Hall of Heroes</b> or <b>Elysian Few.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T02:09:12-07:00","id":210991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Their powers are &quot;Pactio&quot; (for the moment), and represent bargains and deals that they've made with the entities of the Dark Forest (hobgoblins, changelings, the occasional Exile). I'm thinking they should have Drawbacks and catches. And they might even have heavy prices that they have to pay to learn the Pact, similar to how Goblin Markets work. </div> </div> </div>You could adapt the pledge system for the Endowments, similar to how Goblin Vows work. And the more dots in it, the better deal the character may get (but never for free).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 07-28-2014, 05:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T03:29:31-07:00","id":211030,"title":"","content":"The Descendants<br /> The \u201cmythic\u201d Heroes of history are not myths. People like Heracles, Achilles, Beowulf, Gilgamesh and Sigurd were all real people, and they all battled real creatures. Their deeds have become myth and legend as time has passed, but in truth their legacies live on today. Heroic blood flows through a surprising number of veins, though most will never know. Some will feel the pull towards greatness, taking courage in moments of crisis while others are paralyzed in fear. Many become soldiers, and in moments of impossible adversity find themselves without fatigue or shred of fear. Others, the cursed few, find themselves called to the dark places, still slick with blood, to the lair of Grendel or to the hydra\u2019s swamp. These souls were born to glory, fighting the things that should not be.<br /> <br /> Life with the blood of a hero is measured in shining moments of glory, in blood soaked carnage and in savage scars. We Descendants fight battles that will never be told of, against things the world refuses to believe in. Our names shall never be spoken of in the same way others speak of our ancestors, but the creatures of hunger and blood mark them well. We are the Descendants, and our blood calls to yours; welcome home, hero.<br /> <br /> Endowment: Heritage 0-00000 Each dot allows for the selection of a single Heritage power.<br /> <br /> <b>Fear no Beast:</b> Your ancestor stared down all manner of terrible creature without flinching. Over the years this might has decayed, allowing the Descendant to ignore the effects of a single breed of beast. (+ 2 to Resist Lunacy, Success grants a single Beat)<br /> <b>Steadfast Will:</b> A hero's will never flags, their stride never falters, and this trait has carried down through the generations. Not as indomitable as it once was, your heritage still provides some measure of protection. (+2 to resist \u201cnormal\u201d coercion, restore 1 point of Willpower when successful)<br /> <b>Visionary: </b>Heroes throughout time have been gifted with glimpses of things yet to come. Time has worn down the strength of this foresight, but it still offers some benefit for Descendants. (I'd like it to add to skill rolls/defense)<br /> <b>Purified Blood:</b> Many heroes claimed divine parentage, this power harkens back to those deific founders. In modern nights the divinity of blood is less potent, but it still holds power beyond that of a mortal. (Whenever something attempts to drink your blood they suffer 1 Aggravated wound for every point of damage they inflict.)<br /> <b>Mighty Thews: </b>Hercules, Odysseus, Ajax and many other heroes are remarked to have had strength beyond that of mere mortals. As you are descended from these legends, some measure of their strength resonates within you. (Whenever you risk willpower on a Strength based roll, add an additional 2 dice to the roll, increase willpower restored on success by 1.)<br /> <b>Legendary Endurance:</b> The legends and stories speak of how heroes can shrug off wounds that would kill lesser men. There is truth to this claim, as the blood now coursing through your body strengthens it against all assaults. (Permanently increase Health by 2 boxes)<br /> <b>Fierce Defiance</b>: Even when forced to submit, a hero's inner strength will eventually shatter all that bind it. Your will is strong, but it is only an echo of the power once held by your ancestors. (By spending a willpower point, a Descendant may attempt another resistance roll against any ongoing mental manipulation)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T11:31:32-07:00","id":216042,"title":"","content":"Here's a Fae focused Conspiracy I wrote up a while back:<br /> <br /> <b>Dead Man's Hand</b><br /> <br /> They came into his parlor, card counters and double shufflers. They strutted down his street, inside traders and ponzi schemers. He watched them, cultivated them, and eventually collected the best of them. He marched them through the back doors of casinos, out the front doors of broker offices, and he offered them all a choice. Face justice; broken kneecaps, hard time; or sign on the dotted line. They always signed and he always closed with the same line &quot;Who I am does not matter. I'm no one. Just a ghost. A dead man. And you are my hand.&quot; Then he left them with a number to call if they saw anything interesting.<br /> <br /> They left with their winnings, and the promise that they could go on cheating the system as long as they kept their end of the bargain. It wasn't long before the visions started, the scarlet man with gnashing teeth, the girl made of cherry blossoms and wind. They called and the Dead Man gave them a time and place.<br /> <br /> It came easy to them. They had been doing it all their lives. Lowering peoples guard, earning trust they did not deserve, patiently waiting to pull off the long con and collect when the mark was most vulnerable. The Dead Man told them when and where to deliver the package and done was done. Sometimes he was waiting for them with a bonus, a &quot;contractually stipulated perk for his employees&quot; he said.<br /> <br /> The Dead Man is gangly-thin man with short white hair. He is never seen without a self-rolled cig clenched in his teeth, nor in anything other than a black suit with rust-red pinstripes. Members of the Hand who pick up a bit of Fae Lore believe that his motivations, abilities, and origins have something to do with the ancient broken pact between the Fae and Iron. Theories range from the Dead Man being the Fae personification of Irons wrath, the disgraced Fae who originally broke the deal, or a Wyrd manifestation that resulted from the breach of contract.<br /> <br /> <b>Endowments: The Contract of Broken Vows</b><br /> <br /> (never got around to writing up the Endowment, anyone want to take a stab at it?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3628-deaddude","user":"deaddude","date":". 08-01-2014, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3628-deaddude","name":"deaddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T04:20:01-07:00","id":235294,"title":"","content":"I made a Hunter group that focuses on Changelings and is made up of Magical Girls. The one I mentioned earlier. Based around a TV show that functions half as propaganda and half as a memorial to Hunters who've fallen in fighting the Darkness, they mostly deal with the &quot;Unseelie&quot; fairies that come from beyond &quot;The Dark Forest&quot;, and get their powers from &quot;Seelie&quot; faerie who claim to have been exiled by the Unseelie. I forgot to mention it somewhere in the write up, so I should go rewrite it, but they're basically working for Exiled True Fae to toss a wrench into anything the others do.<br /> <br /> I need some more Endowments for them. I mostly used the format of Ink, and it's hard trying not to take powers from either Ink or <i>Princess</i>. In the end I did take the name Barrier Jacket, and I did merge Kensai/Empty Hands/Levinbolt into one weapon. Almost everything the Guardians deal with is a 1 to 1 for Changeling stuff. Unseelie are True Fae, Seelie are Exiles, Doppelgangers are Fetches. The Dark Forest is the Hedge, and technically their Safe Houses in the Hedge are Hallows.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/IPOPtJx.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Everyone dreams when they\u2019re little of being something more. Firemen, police officers, superheroes, princesses. When we\u2019re younger, we always think that adults can do amazing things, and we always wish we had some kind of power to change things. For many children since the late 90s, they grew up wanting to be <i>Starlight Guardians</i>, first a comic book series created by Kagome Yuzuki, a young Japanese woman living in LA, and then later as a Saturday morning cartoon. It was standard fare, well received. A story about young girls who fought against nightmares and a vaguely defined \u201cDarkness\u201d. The themes all centered on friendship and companions and it was praised for the fact that the girls struggled with protecting the world and going to school, as opposed to most other shows where classes are never missed and family is never worried.<br /> It was considered a deconstruction of the magical girl genre, showing what the fallout might be, but it remained hopeful and upbeat, and managed to find an audience across many age groups and demographics.<br /> Yuzuki has never really given an interview, despite her creation being so popular, licensed, translated, and dubbed in several languages. <i>Starlight Guardian</i> cosplay is common at anime and comic book conventions, and there have even been six video games and two stage musicals in Japan. All that\u2019s known about her is that she moved to LA when she was 16, and that she\u2019d been disabled when she was 19. Some fans speculate that she was shot, but there\u2019s nothing but rumour to support that, certainly not medical records.<br /> The truth is that Yuzuki <i>didn\u2019t</i> come up with the <i>Starlight Guardians</i> and their secret world of magic and fairy creatures. They\u2019re a Conspiracy of Hunters, mostly young women, dedicated to fighting evil and stopping the creatures that live in the Dark Forest, that cause nightmares and steal away children. She belonged to them once, and they\u2019re very real. They really do fight against darkness, creating citadels and fortresses in the magical realm known as the Dark Forest. They gain their powers by making deals with the creatures that live there that <i>don\u2019t</i> want to devour the living, or cause nightmares. Everything written about in the comics is based on the experiences of Yuzuki and her cell, and later on stories she heard from other magical girls.<br /> Originally it was a way of coping with her injuries, which left her unable to fight. As time went on, the Starlight Guardians have used Yuzuki\u2019s rather sizable media empire, rivaling that of Sanrio (of Hello Kitty fame) to act as a sort of propaganda. Young women take to the idea more easily when they can point to something. For many of them, their secret becomes a shared experience. Some turn away from the show, hating it. Others love the comics and cartoons, and hope that Yuzuki will immortalize their exploits so that they can encourage other young girls to be heroes.<br /> Kagome herself is now in her twilight years, an unassuming Asian woman in her mid eighties. She works with the Guardians still, though rarely as anything other than a figurehead. She doesn\u2019t lead, and she sleeps with a gun underneath her pillow.<br /> The girls who join the Conspiracy are often young. Younger than most other Conspiracies by a long shot. Some are barely out of middle school. While most are high schoolers, there are some who make it to college before they\u2019ve been brought into the fold. Almost every Starlight Guardian has had an interaction with the Unseelie, evil faeries from beyond the Dark Forest who feed on mortal children and pervert dreams. Some lost friends and loved ones, while others were taken themselves, and still bear the scars as their skin was torn at by the thorns before their rescue.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#003300\"><span style=\"font-family:Rackham\"><b>The Dark Forest</b></span></span><br /> The magical girls make their sanctuary in the Dark Forest, a dreamscape wilderness with all manner of strange entities. Much of it isn\u2019t actual forest, but all throughout even the strange towns and markets are vines and branches, and the ever present thorns. All manner of faerie beastie lives in the Forest, some strange animals that almost but not quite look like mundane animals. Some of the stranger creatures can even talk. And in sometimes in little temples or caves, or even in the markets, the Starlight Guardians can find something even more powerful.<br /> They call them the Seelie. They claim to have been banished from their homes by the Unseelie, and they bargain with the Guardians, granting them powers to fight the Unseelie that manage to get to earth, stopping them from grabbing up children. Many of the Guardians have personal grudges against the Unseelie as well, for replacing siblings with doppelgangers, or trying to grab them through the Thorns.<br /> Many of the magical girls can sculpt the Dark Forest, creating new pathways that are safe, and even creating little bastions of hope against the darkness.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#003300\"><span style=\"font-family:Rackham\"><b>The Enemy</b></span></span><br /> The Unseelie are everywhere because the Dark Forest is everywhere. They poison dreams and steal away the innocent. Many a Starlight Guardian was born when a young woman was dragged out of bed at night and found herself pulled through the thorns of the Dark Forest, only to be rescued from whatever horrid fate awaited her in some far away faerie castle by an upperclasswoman who always seemed so distant and aloof. The Guardians make their Safe Houses far away from mortal eyes in the Dark Forest, and they do fight the nightmare beings there sometimes, but more often than not they chase down the monsters that creep out of the Dark Forest and threaten the innocent.<br /> Monsters of all stripes have their origins in the Dark Forest, from creepy crawly spidery things that hide in attics and wait to capture anyone exploring that old abandoned house, to strange batlike things that glide through the night sky. While faeries that steal away children are the primary enemy, more often than not the magical girls face inhuman creatures, animals that escaped the Forest and try to sate their hungers.<br /> There are also many doppelgangers, people left behind when the Unseelie take someone away. They often don\u2019t even know what they are, and the Guardians are torn on how to deal with them. Some feel that as creatures of the Dark Forest they should either be destroyed--often resulting in the doppelganger turning into a pile of sticks and stones and snails and puppy dog tails--or sent back into the Dark Forest by force. Others feel that they\u2019re as much victims as those who are stolen away, and that killing them just tears a family apart. At least with a doppelganger they think their son or mother or relative is alright.<br /> Sometimes, the Seelie beings that the Starlight Guardians make pacts with will have certain tasks for them. Sometimes finding rare ingredients, or dealing with the Hobgoblins in the Dark Forest itself, before they can even leave it. Most of them have no problem carrying out these \u2018missions\u2019.<br /> Even beyond the Unseelie and the monsters that crawl out of the Dark Forest, there are many other things that feed on the innocent. No magical girl worth her salt would ever refuse to fight an enemy because it\u2019s \u201cnot my problem\u201d.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#003300\"><span style=\"font-family:Rackham\"><b>Hunters</b></span></span><br /> College was a big change. You\u2019d just gotten out of a bad relationship, you were away from home for the first time. You were on your own. At first you were okay with it, but as the weeks went on, your dreams became nightmares, all the horrors of loneliness magnified. They all came to a head when you were dragged out of your bed by a woman on horseback, her hair--her <i>head</i>--all on fire. She dragged you by the ankles and your flannel nightgown was torn to ribbons and your skin was bleeding, but before she could steal you away for good you were rescued. Now you work to keep others from experiencing what you did.<br /> You absolutely adored <i>Starlight Guardians</i>. It was your favourite show as a kid, you had all the toys, and even now you have a plushy of Hitomi, but as you got older you grew out of it, and called it kids stuff. That was before you were attacked in the park one night by a creature that looked like something out of a nightmare--or a TV show. Then a little white creature asked \u201cDo you want to be a Starlight Guardian?\u201d Now you\u2019re living your dream, and you know twelve year old you would cream herself, but you just wish you could sleep soundly ever again.<br /> You\u2019re a guy. Not a macho guy, but you always thought there was something wrong with the guys who obsessed over a cartoon for girls. Then you accidentally wandered into the Dark Forest somehow, and you were drafted. Now you obsess over the cartoon yourself, hoping that it will give you some idea of how to keep from dying now that you know there are monsters out there. And you <i>really</i> wish you\u2019d listen to your mom when she said to cut your hair.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#003300\"><span style=\"font-family:Rackham\"><b>Circles</b></span></span><br /> The Starlight Guardians aren\u2019t a unanimous group. There are several smaller groups that make up the Conspiracy, each with a different way of approaching the Vigil. Within the Conspiracy, they\u2019re known as \u201ccircles\u201d, after the group of doujinshi artists.<br /> <b>Big Sisters, Little Sisters</b> is a group of magical girls who focus not so much on the Dark Forest or fighting monsters, but on helping those less fortunate. They even have a public face, acting openly as fans of theStarlight Guardians, dressing up in cosplay, and visiting sick children. They even put on skits at elementary schools. They believe they can make the world a safer place by making it less hospitable to the nightmare sustained Unseelie.<br /> Spreading information through doujinshi and fanfiction, as well as helping with the animated series, <b>Starlight Projekt</b> can help get the word out on tactics and chronicle the exploits of Guardians. Sometimes they even honour fallen Guardians, though they do have a tendency to dramatize events and \u201cship\u201d members of the Conspiracy. They also manage to bring in money for the magical girls. Kagome Yuzuki belongs to this circle.<br /> The largest circle within the Guardians is the<b> Starlight Sisterhood</b>, who actually go out and fight the monsters up close and personal. Many of it do it out of a sense of justice, or regret at not being able to save a sibling. But a rather large number simply want to show up in one of Starlight Projekt\u2019s doujinshi, or be immortalized by Yuzuki herself in the cartoon that inspired most of them to fight in the first place.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#003300\"><span style=\"font-family:Rackham\"><b>Status</b></span></span><br /> Status in the Sisterhood is gained by stopping evil, and by the number of pacts and agreements with the things in the Dark Forest.<br /> \u25cf Entry into the Guardians comes from first defeating one of the evil faeries. You can purchase dots of Pactio, and have others who can look up to you.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf You\u2019ve seen enough of the things that haunt nightmares that you know how to recognize them. You gain the Unseen Sense Merit fromThe God-Machine Chroniclep.175 towards the Fae.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf At the highest level of Status within the Conspiracy, you have several resources to call upon thanks to your pacts and bargains with your Sisters. Divide three dots however you like between Allies, Retainer, or Safehouse Merits.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#003300\"><span style=\"font-family:Rackham\"><b>New Endowment: Pactio</b></span></span><br /> By making deals with the more benign creatures of the Dark Forest, the Starlight Sisterhood gains some measure of supernatural power to do battle with the creatures of nightmares. Every time a member of the Starlight Guardians gains a new dot of Pactio, choose one of the following Endowments. A Guardian can change out which Pactio powers she has by sleeping for one night in the Dark Forest. Each point of Pactio comes with a cost, though: The magical girl takes on a Ban as if she were a Rank 1 spirit for each dot, representing the bargains made with the Seelie that allow her to use the powers. Her magic also suffers a specific Bane: Cold Iron.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#003300\"><span style=\"font-family:Rackham\"><b>Mascot</b></span></span><br /> Something from the Dark Forest agrees to help the magical girl, whether out of the goodness of it\u2019s heart(?) or because she\u2019s made a bargain with it. The mascot is rarely larger than a dog, and looks nothing like a normal animal. It understands simple commands, and will carry them out, though more complex actions might require a Presence + Animal Ken roll.<br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/KI1YHTj.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <b>Attributes:</b> 3/3/2 (divide among Power, Finesse, Resistance)<br /> <b>Skills:</b> 9/7/3 (divide among Mental, Physical, Social)<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> Power + Resistance<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 10 (10 max), used for casting Dread Powers.<br /> <b>Speed:</b> Strength + Dexterity + Species Factor<br /> <b>Defense:</b> Lower of Dexterity or Wits, plus Athletics<br /> <b>Health:</b> Stamina + Size.<br /> <b>Virtue and Vice:</b> Any. Some Mascots share the magical girl\u2019s Virtue, while others might not.<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5 or less, based on the animal it mocks<br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b>Assign four dots<br /> <b>Innocuous:</b> Anyone but it\u2019s magical girl suffers -2 to Perception rolls to notice the Mascot.<br /> <b>Conditions: </b>The bonded Guardian and the Dark Forests are considered suitable conditions for regaining Essence. Any time a Mascot resolves a condition, or would otherwise gain a Beat, it instead gains a point of Essence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#003300\"><span style=\"font-family:Rackham\"><b>Barrier Jacket</b></span></span><br /> Battling evil is a tough job, and anything that you could call \u201cevil\u201d with a straight face generally isn\u2019t going to pull punches, even against a teenage girl. The Barrier Jacket is a lightweight piece of armour that protects a Starlight Guardian. By spending a point of Willpower as a Reflexive action, she gains an armour rating equal to her Resolve for the scene.<br /> The \u201cJacket\u201d covers her entire body, though it may not look it. It often takes the form of a cheerleading outfit or school uniform, and has touches of glittery moonlight in it. No matter what appearance the barrier jacket takes, it provides complete protection for the scene and is impossible to hide as mundane. Cold iron ignores the Barrier Jacket\u2019s armour.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#003300\"><span style=\"font-family:Rackham\"><b>Light of Truth</b></span></span><br /> A bright light shines from the Guardian, centered on her heart. It emanates around her and reaches out a number of yards equal to her Presence, illuminating the area as if it were a flickering candle. In addition to creating light, anyone within the radius of the light talking to the magical girl must spend a point of Willpower to speak falsely, and takes a -2 to any rolls to obfuscate the truth. In addition, any supernatural creatures roll Composure + Potency contested by the Guardian\u2019s Presence + Resolve to remain hidden, whether through invisibility or stealth. Mundane characters are spotted instantly. The light also causes hidden nooks and crannies to glow faintly, giving anyone looking for hidden objects a +3 to their rolls.<br /> A character must concentrate when using the Light of Truth, and can take no other actions besides moving her speed and using her Defense.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#003300\"><span style=\"font-family:Rackham\"><b>Costume Weapon</b></span></span><br /> No magical girl would be complete without a fancy sword or bow and arrow. By spending a point of Willpower, the Starlight Guardian summons a physical weapon that uses the Weaponry skill and takes the form of a staff, a mystical sword, or something of the type. The weapon is between size 1 and 4 with a damage rating of 1L, and an initiative penalty of -0.<br /> The weapon lasts for a single scene, and can never be lost or stolen. Any time it isn\u2019t in the Guardian\u2019s hand, she can summon it right back at the top of the initiative.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#003300\"><span style=\"font-family:Rackham\"><b>Light Steps</b></span></span><br /> Sometimes monsters can get places that people normally can\u2019t. By making this bargain, a magical girl can reach those places as well. Provided she moves at double her speed, she can move along any surface, even one that couldn\u2019t support her weight or is against gravity. A Guardian with this power can run up walls, across glass, or even over deep mud or shifting sand (but not water) without so much as ruining her shoes. When using this power, she can also leap incredible distances, doubling her successes on any such Athletics rolls.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#003300\"><span style=\"font-family:Rackham\"><b>Big Sister Says</b></span></span><br /> Blessed by the inner light--or at least the pacts with the Seelie--the magical girls can resonate an aura of authority. By spending a point of Willpower and rolling Presence + Intimidation + Striking Looks versus each opponent\u2019s Composure + Potency, a Starlight Guardian can make herself appear to be someone more imposing or authoritative. She doesn\u2019t <i>actually</i> become anyone different, but people <i>perceive</i> her as being in charge so long as she doesn\u2019t do anything to go against that impression.<br /> In addition, so long as she doesn\u2019t openly carry a weapon or strike at anyone, if an opponent does choose to attack her, they first have to spend a point of Willpower and roll Resolve + Composure.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#003300\"><span style=\"font-family:Rackham\"><b>Love Love Beam</b></span></span><br /> Originally this Pactio ability had a different name, but the silly one stuck after it showed up in a <i>gaiden</i> or sidestory in the original <i>Starlight Guardian</i> comic. Older or more uptight Guardians prefer to call it the Starlight Beam. It takes the form of a magical burst of light coming out of the magical girl\u2019s chest or hand (though more than one Guardian has shot hers out of her mouth) with the spending of a point of Willpower and a roll of Dexterity + Athletics. The blast has a damage rating of 2 and does only bashing damage, but it ignores Defense. The short range for the Love Love Beam a number of yards equal to the magical girl\u2019s Presence + Resolve.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#003300\"><span style=\"font-family:Rackham\"><b>Knockout Punch</b></span></span><br /> Sometimes enemies don\u2019t stay down. Those enemies that just keep on coming just need a little assistance getting flat on their ass. By spending a point of Willpower for the rest of the scene the Guardian\u2019s fists are cloaked in magic, or perhaps starry gauntlets appear. Any brawling attacks that she takes now do an additional 1 bashing damage on a successful hit, and the first time an opponent is hit they suffer the Knockdown Tilt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":".  Added powers 08-21-2014, 01:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T05:06:00-07:00","id":235313,"title":"","content":"It's not anything which has an elaborate write-up, just few general concept I would like to expand at some point.<br /> <br /> SaucerWatch, ported from Delta Green and given NWoD twist. A compact that pursues the proof of alien abductions worldwide. Believes that Changelings are nothing more than poor victims of UFO abductions that need help, support and therapy, and any strange about them is result of insidious aliens tampering with their DNA. And any substitutes that replaced Changelings are clearly nepharious clones trying to infiltrate human society for their alien masters!<br /> <br /> Majestic-12 gets a port as well as a conspiracy. A government agency fooled by a group of True Fae into thinking they are aliens trying to establish relations with the government. Higher echelons know about the abduction and are bribed by True Fae to keep mouths shut and help covering up evidence in exchange for 'alien technology'. Probably Fae are not interacting directly, but through constructs that resemble aliens. <br /> <br /> Unnamed yet compact, a family that has been hunting Vampires for countless generations. The twist? Family sticks together and hunts together, even beyond death. Basically, the ancestor spirits help their descendants wage feud on a group of Vampires. Equipped with necromantic sorcery by their ancestors, they are puppets in a shadow game between old spirits and hoary Vampire elders (their childer being puppets as well).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T11:25:08-07:00","id":235598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=235294#post235294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need some more Endowments for them. I mostly used the format of Ink, and it's hard trying not to take powers from either Ink or <i>Princess</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div> Go ahead, stealing is encouraged from everything I write - Picasso said it best.<br /> <br /> I might try and put a sneeky shout out into Princess somewhere, but for for obvious reasons I'm not going to actually include them.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T22:05:00-07:00","id":236184,"title":"","content":"Added a few more powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T11:15:53-07:00","id":236714,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of the half breeds banding together to stop being used by their full template...cousins, lords, parents...etc. it would be too heavily crossed over for most, but since in my game, the high fantasy shard-world templates exist in normal nwod-a cell might be-a dhampir, two wolf-blooded siblings, two heroic mortals, and a second sight medium focusing on ghosts. The dhampir doesnt want to be a vampire's pet/errand boy, the wolf blooded dont want to be eaten by the pure or turned out to breed by the forsaken, the heroics want to slay the ogres and dragons or whatever changling stuff they have encountered, and the medium wants to know why the geist wont let them help the ghosts in that house pass on. Throw in demon blooded or stigmatics, atlanteans, the wolf like beings from mirrors, or perhaps even a prommy that has reached humanity...whatevs. not really a practical compact...but a large enough group of the lesser templates could be impressively effective at the vigil or possibly shake up the power structure of a city..well...town.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T13:46:56-07:00","id":236896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=235313#post235313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unnamed yet compact, a family that has been hunting Vampires for countless generations. The twist? Family sticks together and hunts together, even beyond death. Basically, the ancestor spirits help their descendants wage feud on a group of Vampires. Equipped with necromantic sorcery by their ancestors, they are puppets in a shadow game between old spirits and hoary Vampire elders (their childer being puppets as well).</div> </div> </div> </div>If this were a conspiracy that did an AssCreed-style &quot;inherit an ancestor's skills at risk of insanity,&quot; I'd be well and truly in love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T14:19:43-07:00","id":236924,"title":"","content":"It is a pretty sweet idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T14:31:14-07:00","id":236930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If this were a conspiracy that did an AssCreed-style &quot;inherit an ancestor's skills at risk of insanity,&quot; I'd be well and truly in love. </div> </div> </div>Sure why not, but I did not play Assassin's Creed, so I cannot say more. Just feel free to mod it as you like <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T14:46:55-07:00","id":236957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I made a Hunter group that focuses on Changelings and is made up of Magical Girls. The one I mentioned earlier. Based around a TV show that functions half as propaganda and half as a memorial to Hunters who've fallen in fighting the Darkness, they mostly deal with the &quot;Unseelie&quot; fairies that come from beyond &quot;The Dark Forest&quot;, and get their powers from &quot;Seelie&quot; faerie who claim to have been exiled by the Unseelie. I forgot to mention it somewhere in the write up, so I should go rewrite it, but they're basically working for Exiled True Fae to toss a wrench into anything the others do. </div> </div> </div>I cannot help but thinking in this:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/3OvLP.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T11:28:06-07:00","id":237173,"title":"","content":"Completely trustworthy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T01:54:33-07:00","id":240036,"title":"","content":"I still haven't gotten through the first episode of Magical Meguca yet, but Kyubey was basically what I had in mind with the Pactio Endowment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T10:57:18-07:00","id":245461,"title":"","content":"Anyway further elaborating on that compact idea of mine.<br /> <br /> I followed suggestions of other NWoDers, including atamajakki, to make it a conspiracy. <br /> <br /> I also switched from anti-vampire focus to more anti-supernatural in general.<br /> <br /> Reiterating, it's an extended family of Hunters, dating back to times of Roman Republic, who employ necromantic sorcery in their Vigil. Their signature method is letting their ancestor spirits possess their bodies temporarily, granting the experience and abilities of a veteran Hunter to even relatively untested one. The catch to this method is that if botched the spirit may possess the host permamently, gnawing slowly at the sanity of the host and ultimately even displacing the personality of the host for good. <br /> <br /> Who knows if the highest echelons of this conspiracy are actually people from ancient times, just in bodies of their distant descendants?<br /> <br /> Apart from this possession technique, the conspiracy has access to other necromantic techniques, and are not above binding troublesome ghosts they encounter to their service, which according to one Geist player would mean a state of cold-war between this organisation and Sin-Eaters. I don't know much about this line, so I would be glad if Geist people could offer some advice.<br /> <br /> And somebody I know suggested me to make some connection between them and Birds of Minerva, though nothing is set in the stone at this stage, obviously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T17:05:17-07:00","id":245701,"title":"","content":"Les Mysteres has some of the exact same mechanics. I would look them up, they're from Spirit slayers. Just reskin them and you're pretty much golden.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key"