class=\"message\">Apart from this possession technique, the conspiracy has access to other necromantic techniques, and are not above binding troublesome ghosts they encounter to their service, which according to one Geist player would mean a state of cold-war between this organisation and Sin-Eaters. I don't know much about this line, so I would be glad if Geist people could offer some advice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think of Sin-Eaters as very rare, very powerful, necromancers. Half of whom are weirdoes but not weirder than mortal weirdos, the other half devoutly believe in a some bizarre faith that's clearly made up by mixing lots of different religions and bits of fiction without much logic; half of those religions say that only Sin-Eaters are aloud to be necromancers.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T18:10:34-07:00","id":246484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=245702#post245702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The long and short of it, they have the mechanics for allowing a spirit to half possess them and reap the benefits of it. They're one of my favorite conspiracies, crunch wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T19:15:39-07:00","id":246552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The long and short of it, they have the mechanics for allowing a spirit to half possess them and reap the benefits of it. They're one of my favorite conspiracies, crunch wise. </div> </div> </div>Now that you mention it, my friend remarked that my conspiracy could have some kind of beef with Les Mysteries, but did not elaborate on that further.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T00:07:17-07:00","id":246683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The long and short of it, they have the mechanics for allowing a spirit to half possess them and reap the benefits of it. They're one of my favorite conspiracies, crunch wise. </div> </div> </div>My only complain is, I would have prefered their endowments less &quot;fixed&quot; and more of an open system, depending of what spirits they were bargaining with, while leaving the low-level power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T13:20:28-07:00","id":247094,"title":"","content":"Why not reskin <a href=\"http://hunter-the-vigil-cults.wikia.com/wiki/Chapter_Four:_Theology#Devotion\" target=\"_blank\">Devotion</a>? You'd still need a list of powers, but that's easily handled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T13:33:58-07:00","id":479425,"title":"","content":"Hey! While most of my Hunter knowledge is second-hand, I've had some ideas I though it would be neat to share. Not sure if some of these guys would be better as Compacts or Conspiracies. The names in parenthesizes are names I acknowledge are probably stupid and need to change. Sorry if this is &quot;thread necromancy&quot;(after all, I know how y'all feel about witches! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> \u2022&quot;Arbitrators&quot;: Not all groups of Hunters have a particularly martial bent, and the Arbitrators number amongst them. Instead they prefer to broker more equitable relationships for all. Why waste time and effort hunting, they ask the vampire, when the group can get them regular donations and willing groupies, so long as the vampire treats them right....and makes sure to sign on the bottom line, of course. Because, for all the group's smiles and kindness, they learned the group's Endowment, their understanding of oaths and bindings, from beings born of brimstone and brambles; if you value your life, your sanity, your very soul.... make sure to keep you side of the deal.<br /> <br /> \u2022&quot;The Cult of the Dog&quot;: The group was originally founded by a group of Wolf-blooded who managed to escape from a Pure breeding camp, who ended up allying with each other in order to survive. Over the years, their focus and recruiting have expanded, lashing out against groups that would tear down civilization, from Predator Kings and nostalgic Arisen to a group of &quot;mere&quot; ecoterrorists who want to return humanity to the stone age. Despite their seemingly &quot;domesticated&quot; mission, the group tends towards the aggressive, not helped by an Endowment, a process known to them as &quot;Feralization&quot;, which grants them physical potency at exchange for making them more animistic.<br /> <br /> \u2022Association for the Preservation of Abnormality: This one is decidedly a Compact. More specifically, it's a group created to support and aid fellow &quot;abnormals&quot;, that is, people who possess Supernatural merits or &quot;Independent&quot; minor templates(Offspring and Wolf-blooded could be members, but Ghouls couldn't, if that makes sense?). The group is involved with the Vigil in order to better reach out to fellow abnormals and because they're so often forced to defend themselves from &quot;bigger&quot; supernaturals that now they want to go on the offensive.*<br /> <br /> \u2022The Crossroads Society: An organization founded through a merger of the more dedicated members of the Silent Imperative and a few Ghouls and Kindred who foretold the fall of the Gallows Post. The group focuses on &quot;under the table&quot; transportation, ferrying people and objects place-to-place discreetly and without question(for a small fee, of course). They also specialize in the &quot;Otherworlds&quot;, such as the Hedge and the Great Below, using them as specialized shortcuts, and are somewhat infamous amongst the Vigil for their willingness to work with monsters.<br /> <br /> \u2022Arm of the Angels: This group dates itself back to the dark ages, where the G-M sent one of its Psychopomps to pretend to be an angel of God in order to convince a small, isolated village to produce some needed Infrastructure. But one of the villagers ended up becoming Stigmatic, and in the resulting fever dreams received what he believed to be a vision of the Archangels, who told him that the &quot;angel&quot; that had enslaved his village was actually a demon in service to the great Machine, Lucifer himself, and charged him to oppose the adversary. Emboldened and furious, he brought the others to his point of view(helped by the fact that the vision had granted him his first dot in the yet- unborn group's Endowment) and led them in killing the cultist who had brought the demon into the universe, and the Infrastructure keeping it alive as well. In that moment, the villagers founded the Conspiracy, swearing an oath to destroy the dark rites Satan needed to work his filth in our world. Today, they exist as a loosely organized collection of Christian &quot;freedom fighters&quot;(and we all know what they say about Freedom Fighters) arranged against the G-M and its works. While I'm not sure how they might work mechanically, their Endowment(let's call it the &quot;Angelic Approbations&quot;) work in a way disturbingly similar to manifesting a Demonic Form Power, each themed after a different angel of traditional mysticism.<br /> <br /> \u2022&quot;The Chaos Theorem&quot;: The group known as the Chaos Theorem, based around a small book of the same name, believes that disorder is necessary. They might not like chaos, or they even might gear it, but all believe that if the universe ever goes beyond a certain threshold of order, the universe will stagnate and die. Therefore, the group has dedicated itself to ensuring the world is kept safe from this fate, overturning long-held structures and disrupting older systems. This puts them at odds with supernaturals such as the Invictus, the Seers, and, most of all, the Machine, who they believe is the personification of Order, who wants to calcify the world out of spite against organic life, which is far too messy for its tastes. Their Endowment would be &quot;Irrational Numerology&quot;, a number of complex equation-koans that allow for limited direction of the localized chaos.<br /> <br /> \u2022The Sybil Selection: More of a &quot;Convention&quot;, as some on this forum would call it, than a Conspiracy, this group is united by the fact that all it's members are prophets...sort-of. Inspired when I read the Wikipedia page for a tv show called Early Edition(about a man who receives tomorrow's newspaper, today!), members receive hints and prophecies from an unknown source in a number of odd ways, from newspapers that haven't been printed yet to websites that don't exist, and are forced into the Vigil lest they be overwhelmed by insistent messages. Their Endowment would obviously be this prophetic talent, and the information it allows them to access, from the name of a murderer burnt on their toast to a phone call from a unknown number that calmly explains that there's an invisible vampire in the room.<br /> <br /> \u2022The Game: This group, I feel I need to note, was inspired by LostLight's work on converting The Union into a Conspiracy. As far as most people are concerned, The Game is a mundane, if worldwide, Augmented Reality scavenger hunt. But some people look closer. Maybe they want to win more than anything, maybe they need something and they'll do anything to get it, or maybe they just stumble into it. Bur whatever the reason, these Players get invited to the &quot;True Game&quot;. By completing various Contests, they get Points, which can be redeemed for a number of(sometimes eerily personalized) Prizes, some mundane, others not. Want enough money to buy and sell your boss? There's a prize for that! Want the impossible to find medicine that can stop the supposedly incurable disease that's killing your daughter?*There's a prize for that! Want the vampire blood you need to ensure your immortality? There's a prize for that! And so, Players are slowly drawn into the Vigil, as Contests transition from &quot;Solve this riddle&quot; and &quot;translate this passage from Sumerian to French&quot; to &quot;Kill this Vampire&quot; and &quot;Stop this human sacrifice&quot;.*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":". 04-13-2015, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T06:18:21-07:00","id":480133,"title":"","content":"Glad to see you liked my Union! The Game is really what I had in mind for their conspiracy level- so you have my blessing at using it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T17:34:26-07:00","id":481739,"title":"","content":"The <b>Dead Musicians</b> are a Conspiracy consisting of musicians, grave-diggers, and mediums; founded in Weimar-era Germany and ousted as the Third Reich rose to power, their unifying feature is that they can hear the <i>Totentanz</i>, the Dance of Death. They see themselves as help for the natural sequence of things; &quot;unscheduled&quot; deaths ruin the Dance nearby, as do the walking dead and the unnaturally alive. Their Endowment, also referred to as <i>Totentanz</i>, sharpens their sensitivity to the music; while any of them can hear murders and death by Supernatural causes, it takes real training to hear corpses in their hiding places, deafen the undead with a whistle, or put down an angry ghost with a violin.<br /> <br /> <i>I keep having a mental image of Hunters going out to hunt zombies with a string quartet pop up; these guys came out of it. On a more serious level, there's a </i>long<i> association of death with music, so I think these guys are thematically solid. It'll also be nice to see a German Conspiracy/Compact that didn't have its start in thanks to the Nazis.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T17:54:48-07:00","id":481789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=481739#post481739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <b>Dead Musicians</b> are a Conspiracy consisting of musicians, grave-diggers, and mediums; founded in Weimar-era Germany and ousted as the Third Reich rose to power, their unifying feature is that they can hear the <i>Totentanz</i>, the Dance of Death. They see themselves as help for the natural sequence of things; &quot;unscheduled&quot; deaths ruin the Dance nearby, as do the walking dead and the unnaturally alive. Their Endowment, also referred to as <i>Totentanz</i>, sharpens their sensitivity to the music; while any of them can hear murders and death by Supernatural causes, it takes real training to hear corpses in their hiding places, deafen the undead with a whistle, or put down an angry ghost with a violin.<br /> <br /> <i>I keep having a mental image of Hunters going out to hunt zombies with a string quartet pop up; these guys came out of it. On a more serious level, there's a </i>long<i> association of death with music, so I think these guys are thematically solid. It'll also be nice to see a German Conspiracy/Compact that didn't have its start in thanks to the Nazis.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Gives me a very Old Kingdoms-esque vibe. Sabriel fighting off a horde of undead crows with whistles and bells. I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T18:40:13-07:00","id":481809,"title":"","content":"That was another inspiration; if I write them up, I might toss some stuff in that lets you copy the Bells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T14:11:14-07:00","id":482763,"title":"","content":"Playing a World of Darkness Abhorsen? That's fantastic. A few of the Bells (Ranna, the Sleeper, leaps to mind) have abilities you don't often see in the game, so it'd be pretty unique. Dulling the senses of undead and maybe even lulling them to sleep is a great little niche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T03:38:34-07:00","id":483387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>amchera:</b> I keep having a mental image of Hunters going out to hunt zombies with a string quartet pop up; these guys came out of it. </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0dfZ9BXaNyE\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0dfZ9BXaNyE</a> (Because it's obligatory to plug Lindsey Stirling whenever an opportunity presents itself). More seriously, I really like this conspiracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T12:07:27-07:00","id":483787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=481739#post481739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <b>Dead Musicians</b> are a Conspiracy consisting of musicians, grave-diggers, and mediums; founded in Weimar-era Germany and ousted as the Third Reich rose to power, their unifying feature is that they can hear the <i>Totentanz</i>, the Dance of Death. They see themselves as help for the natural sequence of things; &quot;unscheduled&quot; deaths ruin the Dance nearby, as do the walking dead and the unnaturally alive. Their Endowment, also referred to as <i>Totentanz</i>, sharpens their sensitivity to the music; while any of them can hear murders and death by Supernatural causes, it takes real training to hear corpses in their hiding places, deafen the undead with a whistle, or put down an angry ghost with a violin.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a really awesome idea.<br /> <br /> You need to state what makes them a Conspiracy though; give them organisation and goals, or at least ideology. That said you could just make them a Comapct with an Endowment, they'd work fine as a Compact.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T14:48:47-07:00","id":483904,"title":"","content":"I just gave some cursory details; I do have an idea for an organization, but its not fleshed out too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T20:46:43-07:00","id":492251,"title":"","content":"I only have a rough idea, but, <b>The Iron Army</b>, a group of modern knights devoted to a mix of the Chivalric Code and a thirst for glory. Their Endowments come in the form of Armory, a mix of supernatural and advanced technological improvements to their armor. At their most advanced they would resemble a cross between King Arthur and Iron Man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T03:19:35-07:00","id":492481,"title":"","content":"So has the upcoming beast given any ideas for a beast centric conspiracy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T05:32:46-07:00","id":492536,"title":"","content":"Not really; but off the top of my head; an Endowed Compact of Gandalf-like mentor figures who specialise in divination, illusion magic, and astral travel. Their goals are, in no particular order.<br /> <br /> 1) Assist Heroes in the hunt.<br /> 2) Teach Heroes how to actually be heroes.<br /> 3) Ensure that the public believes in the idea of heroes.<br /> <br /> In more details.<br /> <br /> 1) They assist heroes by essentially following them around, providing cryptic advice, and secretly working behind the scenes. They understand exactly what the Beast does to a Hero's mind, and while they're sympathetic, or at least they tell each other that they're sympathetic. They also say that they can't heal the Hero so they just play along. For example, rather than using their connections to buy guns for the hero and his followers, they might let slip that arms smugglers will be on the docks tonight. (This would be a lot easier to define once we know more about how heroes work)<br /> <br /> Incidently you ever wondered why Gandalf can't solve problems with his magic. That's why they have illusion powers; it's great for making heroes think they're a powerful wizard shooting lightning bolts but it's really just a pistol. If they fought a beast themselves, well they could use a few tricks like fake walls or duplicating themselves, but in terms of actually hurting the beast they just have a gun. Heroes have, whatever they get.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2) If a Hero thinks he is perfectly capable of judging morality and is willing to do; it's important that they can walk the walk as well as talk the talk. If a Beast is lairng in an orphanage and the Hero has been eying up some petrol cans; find or disguise yourself as an beautiful woman who was fired from the orphanage for trying to stop the Beast and come to the Hero in tears. An instant Quest to rescue the orphans, hopefully next time he'll remember it's Heroic to rescue the kids without prompting, if not Heroes rarely get wise to the beautiful quest giver ruse. (Network Zero has noticed how often Heroes finding themselves rescuing beautiful young philosophy students and keeping them in their entourage).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 3) I'm getting the impression that a Hero's powers come from the collective unconscious of some sort. I imagine the Compact frequently visit The Hero Archetype in the Temenos and make detailed notes of his Behaviour and then they'll call their contacts and make adjustments. If the Hero is too willing to sacrifice faceless extras in order to rescue The Love Interest they'll make sure to put in more scenes where the Hero rescues nameless extras and weaken The Love Interest's hold by writing more one dimensional characters who hang off the Hero's arm and look awestruck. Contrariwise if the Hero is ignoring the Love Interest they'll do the opposite; because it's too useful a way to manipulate real heroes.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think the subgroups will be:<br /> <br /> The Wizard - specialities in behind the scenes work; rather than push the Hero down the path they want, they pave the roads themselves. They create clues for the Hero to solve, and situations for the Hero to react to.<br /> <br /> The Sidekick - they get hands on with the Hero and use psychology to manipulate. They might become the Hero's number two and carefully control what information he receives, pose as a love interest who's impressed by moral behaviour, or a damsel who keeps getting herself captured.<br /> <br /> The Chief - Hero! Turn in your badge now. The Chief poses as the Hero's legitimate superior. If the Hero is a police officer he'll impersonate the chief. He might pretend to be the leader of a secret society of monster hunters who knows the prophecy and insists the Hero works for him now. The Chief uses his minions and resources to support the Hero, but feigned incompetence and reverse psychology is what keeps the Hero on the right road.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't think this group can be written until after the Hero's psychology and powers have been revealed. But for something that I thought up on the spot I think it's a very cool idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T05:07:39-07:00","id":493467,"title":"","content":"Well, I have to say I agree, that is a very interesting idea, although since I get the idea that heroes are obsessive sociopaths playing their minders would be a strenuous job. <br /> <br /> They're going to need a way to fake their own deaths though, mentor occupational hazard and all that. <br /> <br /> But a hunter conspiracy that's about using genre savviness to manipulate things when beasts are about subverting those very tropes, quite nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T10:22:28-07:00","id":493727,"title":"","content":"Compact I think. Despite a hefty if focused Endowment. If your charachter concept is &quot;the puppetmaster behind the scenes&quot; I think it kind of goes against the theme to have a boss ordering your around. So an Endowed Compact it shall be.<br /> <br /> Also I think soceopath isn't quite right; or at least I hope it isn't. I imagine a Hero as someone who has no interest in following any rules or social obligations unless they personally agree with it. However their personal agreement may look like soceopathic &quot;kill the beast and anyone within 100 yards just to make sure&quot; to &quot;Superman esque boyscout&quot;. Hence the Compact's psychological manipulation. If the hero only cares about their personal point of view you better shape that POV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T20:12:53-07:00","id":499695,"title":"","content":"I don't have too much of a structure for this one, but maybe a group whose Endowment is centered around creating masks/disguises allowing themselves to temporarily(so long as nothing goes wrong) tap into a basic human Archetype? Like, if a Child can be Fear of Drowning or Fear of Being Watched, then one of these Hunters could don the identity of the Trickster or Wiseman or Warrior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T05:55:04-07:00","id":500212,"title":"","content":"I'm considering adapting Pact Magic to the Vigil. It would be a nice improvement to Les Mysteres (I find Rites Du Cheval mechanics kinda dull)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T10:10:12-07:00","id":500525,"title":"","content":"Have a look at Dream Catchers in my sig.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T15:36:59-07:00","id":500849,"title":"","content":"Are you talking about the C\u00fa Chulainn Sons and their geas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T04:51:46-07:00","id":502774,"title":"","content":"As well as the Lord Stewards and the Contract Dread Power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T14:10:17-07:00","id":503474,"title":"","content":"Mmm... don\u00b4t fit my views. I was thinking in &quot;making a deal with a spirit/loa of you worship and convince him to posses you in a controllled way, blessing the &quot;horse&quot; with a few bonuses and maybe one or two supernatural powers...but also taking the entity\u00b4s Taboo and Bane for the duration of the whole ordeal.<br /> If the supplicant fails the roll, he would <b>still </b>have the possibility of making the pact...but beware, for he would be forced to making rolls each hour to keeping himself as the dominant personality. Failure would allow the spirit to take control until the Pc archieves an higher roll. <br /> On a dramatic failure the loa would enjoy his new flesh body for a whole day of fun, or until exorcised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T11:21:40-07:00","id":504409,"title":"","content":"An idea for a Compact or Conspiracy that I've been sitting on for a while now is something of a take on The New Inquisition from <i>Unknown Armies</i>. A powerful African-American billionaire driven by an obsessive personal crusade to destroy the forces of darkness had used his considerable resources and connections to form and outfit his own private army to fight this secret war of his. They're not the best and brightest, or else they would've managed to land a legit job. They're the desperate, the downtrodden, the fringe class, the ones willing to do whatever's asked of them in exchange for a steady paycheck and a second chance at life. Their main goal is to track down and eliminate dangerous monsters, but there's another dimension to it beyond keeping the streets safe at night. See, monsters often have money, property, and other assets that their corporate overlord can use to strengthen and expand his own position. What's more, the cell that makes the kill gets a sizable cut of whatever they seize for themselves put right back into their budget, so there's plenty of incentive for them to risk their necks ferreting out well-connected creatures. If they have an Endowment, I'm thinking that it'd be something to let them purchase temporary social merits with this pool of untraceable blood money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3042-weaponwife","name":"WeaponWife","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T19:44:22-07:00","id":1460493,"title":"","content":"Some sort of sikh compact<br /> a compact that hunts flensers<br /> Something similar to the church of the second hythoth<br /> one that tries to assist prometheans in their pilgrimage","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/blob:http://forum.theonyxpath.com/30ff2a5d-ff5b-4dec-8fca-50f9a75f97ea\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <br /> \u201cwhat in the goddamn?\u201d -benny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26749-mothstrigoi","name":"Mothstrigoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T03:42:04-07:00","id":1465883,"title":"","content":"Link to a thread on the same topic: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1379717-general-hunter-groups-fan-made-homebrew-ideas-speculation\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1379717-general-hunter-groups-fan-made-homebrew-ideas-speculation\"> General Hunter Groups, fan-made/homebrew ideas &amp; speculation - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1379717-general-hunter-groups-fan-made-homebrew-ideas-speculation\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1379717-general-hunter-groups-fan-made-homebrew-ideas-speculation </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I'm pretty confident that a thread on this subject has been done before. I found at least one a while ago. However, I have never been able to find it since, which </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T11:35:16-08:00","id":1469006,"title":"","content":"Based (practically stolen) on the comic &quot;Something is Killing the Children&quot; (a comic about Hunters that depicts the horror of the Vigil) i was thinking about a conspiracy of would-be Beasts who instead rebelled against their Horror, ending up sealing it on a guardian against nightmares-and by that i mean their favorite plushie.<br /> <br /> Their endowments would be some sort of reversed Obcasus rites maybe? I know they would have to feed the Horror with fear, and if it was their own fear there would be consequences.<br /> <br /> EDIT: corrected some stupid typing errors. Don't post while sleepy and on your phone kids!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27168-aeneas","user":"Aeneas","date":". 11-29-2021, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27168-aeneas","name":"Aeneas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T16:19:11-08:00","id":1470082,"title":"","content":"A Compact that\u2019s actually an alliance of Hunter Cells filled with scientists and occultists who joined up in the name of both survival, and mutually enlightened self-interest, after managing to piece together enough through mutual communication to begin realising just how <i>deep</i> the rabbit hole is, and are seeking to figure out the \u2018rules\u2019 of the various magic systems.<br /> <br /> The group\u2019s Endowments would typically grant access to info, huge piles of possibly-magical occult nick-knacks, and, if you're really lucky, the good stuff - fully functional magical items with an actual, comprehensible instruction manual on usage, refuelling and maintenance, or even outright education in various minor, but very, <i>very</i> real, sorcerous techniques.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T14:01:41-08:00","id":1470881,"title":"","content":"The two Hunter organizations I've always wanted to create:<br /> <br /> <b>The Black Gun Carnival, The Kingslayer's Game</b><br /> <br /> Loosely inspired by the Stephen Sondheim play Assassins, The Carnival is a compact of killers who murder those of High Status to exchange for prizes with the Proprietor of the Carnival itself, an interstitial space that opens up to those who would be willing to play the game. They usually hunt monsters because the supernatural world has many more kings, queens, sultans, etc. (Status 5 folks) that are more easily accessible than major political figures-which isn't to say that it's all monsters. Benefits include a person's black gun, the use of the carnival for transit and hiding, and of course trading kills of status for prizes. Every time I come around to that last part though, I get hung up on how it works.<br /> <br /> <b>The Heirs to Arcadia</b><br /> <br /> You know the story of how a fairy princess comes to the surface world, gets blinded by the light, and dies, only to reincarnate as a human who, through trial and proof of character, can return to their throne, right? Well, who knows how true that is, but when the ideas for a changeling hunter conspiracy were being batted around, that was always my go to answer-a conspiracy of &quot;princes&quot; and &quot;princesses&quot; tasked by the fairies to brave the iron world and thorn maze to capture and return thieves, deserters, and traitors to their homeland, until such as they've proven their worth. Obviously the take as I'm talking about is a bit on the nose, and I don't want to neccesarily keep it like that-it's more interesting if there's just as much possibility they're right as they are suckers for a Stranger's game, but I always felt like this take was more appropriate than a lot of the other attempts for a changeling hunter conspiracy. Also it lets me riff on Changeling the Dreaming, and is yet another way I would also play with the magical girl idea in Chronicles (because a lot of those early magical girl shows were all about earning or drawing on their royalty).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-22T11:27:16-08:00","id":1471094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=1470881#post1470881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The two Hunter organizations I've always wanted to create:<br /> <br /> <b>The Black Gun Carnival, The Kingslayer's Game</b><br /> <br /> Loosely inspired by the Stephen Sondheim play Assassins, The Carnival is a compact of killers who murder those of High Status to exchange for prizes with the Proprietor of the Carnival itself, an interstitial space that opens up to those who would be willing to play the game. They usually hunt monsters because the supernatural world has many more kings, queens, sultans, etc. (Status 5 folks) that are more easily accessible than major political figures-which isn't to say that it's all monsters. Benefits include a person's black gun, the use of the carnival for transit and hiding, and of course trading kills of status for prizes. Every time I come around to that last part though, I get hung up on how it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could make them gain the Fae-Touched minor template and they trade kills for the ability to spend the exp for Fae-Touched exclusive merits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/213-darkhunter","name":"Darkhunter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar213_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-22T13:57:28-08:00","id":1471102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkhunter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=1471094#post1471094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could make them gain the Fae-Touched minor template and they trade kills for the ability to spend the exp for Fae-Touched exclusive merits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm.....nah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-22T15:34:43-08:00","id":1471106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=1471102#post1471102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>The Heirs to Arcadia</b><br /> <br /> You know the story of how a fairy princess comes to the surface world, gets blinded by the light, and dies, only to reincarnate as a human who, through trial and proof of character, can return to their throne, right? Well, who knows how true that is, but when the ideas for a changeling hunter conspiracy were being batted around, that was always my go to answer-a conspiracy of &quot;princes&quot; and &quot;princesses&quot; tasked by the fairies to brave the iron world and thorn maze to capture and return thieves, deserters, and traitors to their homeland, until such as they've proven their worth. Obviously the take as I'm talking about is a bit on the nose, and I don't want to neccesarily keep it like that-it's more interesting if there's just as much possibility they're right as they are suckers for a Stranger's game, but I always felt like this take was more appropriate than a lot of the other attempts for a changeling hunter conspiracy. Also it lets me riff on Changeling the Dreaming, and is yet another way I would also play with the magical girl idea in Chronicles (because a lot of those early magical girl shows were all about earning or drawing on their royalty).</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this idea enough that it's likely gonna show up in my next Changeling game. Gaslighting mortals and promising them power in return for doing their dirty-work seems like a very Keeper thing to do!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-22T16:32:25-08:00","id":1471109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=1471106#post1471106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like this idea enough that it's likely gonna show up in my next Changeling game. Gaslighting mortals and promising them power in return for doing their dirty-work seems like a very Keeper thing to do!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Unless, of course, it's <i>not</i> just gaslighting.<br /> <br /> Again, I wouldn't want to be too particularly on the nose-even with how unsubtle the monster specific conspiracies of the supplements are, there's still more nuance than the direct pitch of the Heirs have. But I definitely want to build something out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T02:11:20-07:00","id":1476827,"title":"","content":"Okay, I've had a few different basic compact/conspiracy concepts bouncing around inside my skull. Here they are:<br /> <br /> <u>Compacts</u>:<br /> <br /> <b>Ecto-Zone</b>: A collective of mediums, paranormal investigators, and parapsychologists. If ghosts and spirits are bothering you, who you gonna call? These guys. When it's something else though, call somebody else.<br /> <br /> Where the group able to become a Conspiracy, their Endowment would enable them to better understand, communicate with, and if need be, fight with the ethereal.<br /> <br /> <b>The Howling Moon Theatre</b>: A travelling entertainer group, they use the power of dance and song to exorcise malicious ghosts &amp; spirits, imprisoning them within specially prepared masks. They do this by putting on performances that either tell the story of a ghost's life, or that incorporate themes of a spirit's bane/ban.<br /> <br /> As a Conspiracy, they would grow from travelling entertainers to a full-fledged talent agency. Additionally, their Endowment would not only improve their ability to seal way ghosts/spirits but enable them to use the powers of the bound entities by wearing those masks.<br /> <br /> <b>The Neo Ground Railroad</b>: A loose network that specializes in helping others disappear from supernatural foes: a ghoul fleeing an abusive vampire; a changeling wishing to throw a Huntsmen off their trail; a beast that needs to get away from a particularly zealous hero; and many more. These folks have ways of helping others to disappear.<br /> <br /> As a Conspiracy, the NGR would obtain an Endowment that would grant their charges occultion, ward safehouses against unwanted guests, and protect their secrets from supernatural interrogation.<br /> <br /> <u>Conspiracies</u>:<br /> <b>Unusual Investigations</b>: A detective agency that often finds itself involved in jobs that send it's PIs headfirst into the supernatural. Seriously, you'd be surprised how many times a spouse isn't cheating but is in fact a vampire/werewolf/wizard or other something else. Their endowment allows them to track the supernatural, pierce through their lies, and ward off attempts at dissuading them from investigating further.<br /> <br /> <b>Ancestral Wardens</b>: Operating under the guise of ancestry research foundation, the Wardens are a group that studies and reveres the heroes of humanity's past. With their endowment, they call upon the spirits of these legends to aid them in defending humanity from the supernatural, especially the nightmarish beasts which feast on fear and the so-called &quot;heroes&quot; that leave a trail of destruction hunting after them.<br /> <br /> <b>The Burnt Torch Society</b>: A cult that believes fear is not something to flee or fight, but rather something to be embraced. Through embracing their fear, they tap into humankind's most primordial fear: Darkness. Turning the darkness into weapons and armor, they strike fear into those who believe themselves above such feelings.<br /> <br /> <b>JDG Cleaning &amp; Fumigation Incorporated</b>: On the surface, JDG is just another professional cleaning and fumigation company, with their only oddity being that they are a subsidiary of Elysium Cryogenics. Look beneath the surface and you'll discover they perform clean more than windows and deal with far more esoteric pests. Through their Endowment, Projection, their cleaners exit their material bodies and confront haunting ghosts, squatting spirits, and other creatures who think their supernatural powers let them steal other people's real estate. Fans of the Old World of Darkness may find this group familiar...<br /> <br /> Well, this is what I have just off the top of my head, might edit this later with more ideas. What do you guys think?<br /> <br /> ==Edit 1==<br /> Added in what kind of Endowment if my Compacts evolved into Conspiracies. Will add more later.<br /> <br /> ==Edit 2==<br /> Added in JDG Cleaning &amp; Fumigation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":17107,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","user":"Mangaholic13","date":". 03-22-2022, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T04:00:04-07:00","id":1476832,"title":"","content":"I love these ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T18:23:05-07:00","id":1476909,"title":"","content":"Those ideas are pretty good! My favourites have to be Neo Ground Railroad &amp; Ancestral Wardens respectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T02:45:47-07:00","id":1476938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=1476832#post1476832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love these ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrueMrMultiverse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=1476909#post1476909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those ideas are pretty good! My favourites have to be Neo Ground Railroad &amp; Ancestral Wardens respectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>What did you like the most about the NGR and the AW?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":17107,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","user":"Mangaholic13","date":".  Realized how to quote you both... 03-22-2022, 05:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T16:44:57-07:00","id":1477035,"title":"","content":"NGR's neat to me as its concept as a network that helps hide others from supernaturals is quite fascinating and AW's interesting to me with their ability to call upon spirits of legends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T21:28:47-07:00","id":1477054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=1470881#post1470881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The two Hunter organizations I've always wanted to create:<br /> <br /> <b>The Black Gun Carnival, The Kingslayer's Game</b><br /> <br /> Loosely inspired by the Stephen Sondheim play Assassins, The Carnival is a compact of killers who murder those of High Status to exchange for prizes with the Proprietor of the Carnival itself, an interstitial space that opens up to those who would be willing to play the game. They usually hunt monsters because the supernatural world has many more kings, queens, sultans, etc. (Status 5 folks) that are more easily accessible than major political figures-which isn't to say that it's all monsters. Benefits include a person's black gun, the use of the carnival for transit and hiding, and of course trading kills of status for prizes. Every time I come around to that last part though, I get hung up on how it works.<br /> [</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I have an idea, AA, what if it worked like this: What if each time they kill someone Status 5, they get a dot that can be traded for either supernatural prizes (with each prize having a number of dots assigned based how powerful/valuable it is) or can be exchanged for dots in the following Social Merits: Resource, Retainer, Safe Place, Allies, or Contacts.<br /> <br /> Would that work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T23:32:32-07:00","id":1477057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangaholic13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=1477054#post1477054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I have an idea, AA, what if it worked like this: What if each time they kill someone Status 5, they get a dot that can be traded for either supernatural prizes (with each prize having a number of dots assigned based how powerful/valuable it is) or can be exchanged for dots in the following Social Merits: Resource, Retainer, Safe Place, Allies, or Contacts.<br /> <br /> Would that work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ya know, i'mma debate that. That compels me at this hour of day, but I have been moving all of it, so I may be susceptible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T02:32:17-07:00","id":1477065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=1477057#post1477057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue a