m/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=1476827#post1476827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I've had a few different basic compact/conspiracy concepts bouncing around inside my skull. Here they are:<br /> <br /> <u>Compacts</u>:<br /> <br /> <b>Ecto-Zone</b>: A collective of mediums, paranormal investigators, and parapsychologists. If ghosts and spirits are bothering you, who you gonna call? These guys. When it's something else though, call somebody else.<br /> <br /> Where the group able to become a Conspiracy, their Endowment would enable them to better understand, communicate with, and if need be, fight with the ethereal.<br /> <br /> <b>The Howling Moon Theatre</b>: A travelling entertainer group, they use the power of dance and song to exorcise malicious ghosts &amp; spirits, imprisoning them within specially prepared masks. They do this by putting on performances that either tell the story of a ghost's life, or that incorporate themes of a spirit's bane/ban.<br /> <br /> As a Conspiracy, they would grow from travelling entertainers to a full-fledged talent agency. Additionally, their Endowment would not only improve their ability to seal way ghosts/spirits but enable them to use the powers of the bound entities by wearing those masks.<br /> <br /> <b>The Neo Ground Railroad</b>: A loose network that specializes in helping others disappear from supernatural foes: a ghoul fleeing an abusive vampire; a changeling wishing to throw a Huntsmen off their trail; a beast that needs to get away from a particularly zealous hero; and many more. These folks have ways of helping others to disappear.<br /> <br /> As a Conspiracy, the NGR would obtain an Endowment that would grant their charges occultion, ward safehouses against unwanted guests, and protect their secrets from supernatural interrogation.<br /> <br /> <u>Conspiracies</u>:<br /> <b>Unusual Investigations</b>: A detective agency that often finds itself involved in jobs that send it's PIs headfirst into the supernatural. Seriously, you'd be surprised how many times a spouse isn't cheating but is in fact a vampire/werewolf/wizard or other something else. Their endowment allows them to track the supernatural, pierce through their lies, and ward off attempts at dissuading them from investigating further.<br /> <br /> <b>Ancestral Wardens</b>: Operating under the guise of ancestry research foundation, the Wardens are a group that studies and reveres the heroes of humanity's past. With their endowment, they call upon the spirits of these legends to aid them in defending humanity from the supernatural, especially the nightmarish beasts which feast on fear and the so-called &quot;heroes&quot; that leave a trail of destruction hunting after them.<br /> <br /> <b>The Burnt Torch Society</b>: A cult that believes fear is not something to flee or fight, but rather something to be embraced. Through embracing their fear, they tap into humankind's most primordial fear: Darkness. Turning the darkness into weapons and armor, they strike fear into those who believe themselves above such feelings.<br /> <br /> <b>JDG Cleaning &amp; Fumigation Incorporated</b>: On the surface, JDG is just another professional cleaning and fumigation company, with their only oddity being that they are a subsidiary of Elysium Cryogenics. Look beneath the surface and you'll discover they perform clean more than windows and deal with far more esoteric pests. Through their Endowment, Projection, their cleaners exit their material bodies and confront haunting ghosts, squatting spirits, and other creatures who think their supernatural powers let them steal other people's real estate. Fans of the Old World of Darkness may find this group familiar...<br /> <br /> Well, this is what I have just off the top of my head, might edit this later with more ideas. What do you guys think?<br /> <br /> ==Edit 1==<br /> Added in what kind of Endowment if my Compacts evolved into Conspiracies. Will add more later.<br /> <br /> ==Edit 2==<br /> Added in JDG Cleaning &amp; Fumigation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sooooooo.<br /> <br /> It was asked for.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Ecto-Zone</u></b>-Okay, so off hand, what brings these people together to begin with? Without that answered, it sounds like the beginning of idea. I have a harem multi-media project that starts on similar notes. Why are these people brought together, what is expected for their operation, what is their desire for their operation, how in accord are these, and what is the consequence of that?<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Howling Moon Theatre</u></b>-This is way more grounded, and way more interesting, but it still asks a question of why. Since there's a theater aspect to it that excludes privacy (or non-commercial elements, because theatre history is commercially shorter than you remember), and the question of what may be realized with such enactments in relation to Manifestation, Essence satiety*, or other such factors, one has to wonder the element that connects the two. I love, and can really get behind, this notion, but it is <i>sort of</i> needing a very biased perspective that gets you there. I need an ideology, but I also need a person who gets it and tries (and also fails even where it succeeds, but I'm not asking the moon and the stars) and motivates a lot of people beyond the moment.<br /> <br /> <b><u>THe Neo-Ground Railroad</u></b>-Sooooooooooooooo,<br /> <br /> The catch to facilitating and helping with anyone who can help with matters of any given individual organization is that you need to compellingly argue the trust an organization. As a point of comparison, the Ascending Ones have a few <i>millenia</i> of trust and reliance behind their name to facilitate their <i>sulha </i>driven practices of diplomacy between organizations. Since the Neo-Ground Railroad is clearly cribbing off the idea and values of the Underground Railroad in the U.S., it's not lacking on the values of that movement, but it does <i>demand</i> on what can substantiate it, and that means being willing to be controversial. <u><i>Any service that can ensure privacy is one that demands attention.</i></u> You need to make it clear how you can keep your promises, and how your promises can be exploited, and how you try (both successfully and poorly) to address that. And with the standard stated by AO, you need something <i>substantial</i>, something <i>semi-absolute</i>, but also something <i>demonstrably exploitable. </i>So that's a hell of a thread-something so reliable that almost anyone can rely on it, but also how it can be exploited, and how it's currently warded against that, and also also how it can be doubled down on. I <i>want</i> to like this idea, and I can <i>back it</i> so easily as an idea, but it is a bit setting that demands <i>how</i> and <i>why</i> it can happen, and the <i>costs</i> of why it can.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Unusual Investigations</u></b>-So honestly, I like this more from the angle as Hunter Antagonist than as a playable consideration. I'm the person sitting on a STV piece about the The Grand Cult, an Anti-Conspiracy that attempts to unite more and more monster cults together until you create a mass organization allows monsters to rule the world. This feels like a subfunction. I bring this up primarily because it primarily asks the question of if players are expected to play along in the playable sense or not. Hunter is the Anti-EverythingElse Splat because it either A) expects the the character to not get it all, or B)get it and be complicit in it to a certain-but-definitely-drawn degree. Hunters do not have the gamebooks, do not allow them to feel like they do. This is also a problem with the Neo-Ground Railroad.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Ancestral Wardens</u></b>-Jojo's Bizarre Adventure but with Ancestry.com gets a thorough pass from me, no comment, unless somehow the writer does not get it.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Burnt Torch Society</u></b>-I am too much of a Beast fan to argue against this beyond asking a) how does this work, b) how does this relate to monsters, and c) Have you played Alan Wake and have decided to get <i>interesting</i> about all of that?<br /> <br /> <b><u>JDG Cleaning &amp; Fumigation</u></b>-&quot;Why are you not Cheiron?&quot; is my primary stealth criticism.<br /> <br /> And that's why Graaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaass tastes bad.<br /> <br /> *Shut up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T15:12:25-07:00","id":1477365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=1477315#post1477315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sooooooo.<br /> <br /> It was asked for.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Ecto-Zone</u></b>-Okay, so off hand, what brings these people together to begin with? Without that answered, it sounds like the beginning of idea. I have a harem multi-media project that starts on similar notes. Why are these people brought together, what is expected for their operation, what is their desire for their operation, how in accord are these, and what is the consequence of that?<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Howling Moon Theatre</u></b>-This is way more grounded, and way more interesting, but it still asks a question of why. Since there's a theater aspect to it that excludes privacy (or non-commercial elements, because theatre history is commercially shorter than you remember), and the question of what may be realized with such enactments in relation to Manifestation, Essence satiety*, or other such factors, one has to wonder the element that connects the two. I love, and can really get behind, this notion, but it is <i>sort of</i> needing a very biased perspective that gets you there. I need an ideology, but I also need a person who gets it and tries (and also fails even where it succeeds, but I'm not asking the moon and the stars) and motivates a lot of people beyond the moment.<br /> <br /> <b><u>THe Neo-Ground Railroad</u></b>-Sooooooooooooooo,<br /> <br /> The catch to facilitating and helping with anyone who can help with matters of any given individual organization is that you need to compellingly argue the trust an organization. As a point of comparison, the Ascending Ones have a few <i>millenia</i> of trust and reliance behind their name to facilitate their <i>sulha </i>driven practices of diplomacy between organizations. Since the Neo-Ground Railroad is clearly cribbing off the idea and values of the Underground Railroad in the U.S., it's not lacking on the values of that movement, but it does <i>demand</i> on what can substantiate it, and that means being willing to be controversial. <u><i>Any service that can ensure privacy is one that demands attention.</i></u> You need to make it clear how you can keep your promises, and how your promises can be exploited, and how you try (both successfully and poorly) to address that. And with the standard stated by AO, you need something <i>substantial</i>, something <i>semi-absolute</i>, but also something <i>demonstrably exploitable. </i>So that's a hell of a thread-something so reliable that almost anyone can rely on it, but also how it can be exploited, and how it's currently warded against that, and also also how it can be doubled down on. I <i>want</i> to like this idea, and I can <i>back it</i> so easily as an idea, but it is a bit setting that demands <i>how</i> and <i>why</i> it can happen, and the <i>costs</i> of why it can.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Unusual Investigations</u></b>-So honestly, I like this more from the angle as Hunter Antagonist than as a playable consideration. I'm the person sitting on a STV piece about the The Grand Cult, an Anti-Conspiracy that attempts to unite more and more monster cults together until you create a mass organization allows monsters to rule the world. This feels like a subfunction. I bring this up primarily because it primarily asks the question of if players are expected to play along in the playable sense or not. Hunter is the Anti-EverythingElse Splat because it either A) expects the the character to not get it all, or B)get it and be complicit in it to a certain-but-definitely-drawn degree. Hunters do not have the gamebooks, do not allow them to feel like they do. This is also a problem with the Neo-Ground Railroad.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Ancestral Wardens</u></b>-Jojo's Bizarre Adventure but with Ancestry.com gets a thorough pass from me, no comment, unless somehow the writer does not get it.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Burnt Torch Society</u></b>-I am too much of a Beast fan to argue against this beyond asking a) how does this work, b) how does this relate to monsters, and c) Have you played Alan Wake and have decided to get <i>interesting</i> about all of that?<br /> <br /> <b><u>JDG Cleaning &amp; Fumigation</u></b>-&quot;Why are you not Cheiron?&quot; is my primary stealth criticism.<br /> <br /> And that's why Graaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaass tastes bad.<br /> <br /> *Shut up.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right, Arcane Arts, I did ask.<br /> <br /> And I'm glad I've did.<br /> <br /> You've given me much to think about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> <b>Ecto-Zone</b>: You are correct in that the why this group exists is definitely their weakest point. If a group doesn't have a reason why they're working together then it doesn't make any sense. Going off the five questions you posed, I think I might have some vague answers:<br /> <br /> The Compact formed after a particularly nasty haunting forced a Medium, a Paranormal Investigator, and a Parapsychologist to work together in order to solve it; realizing that they were only able to resolve the situation by working together, the group continued to stick together and gradually expanded from there. Their operations bring them to haunted locations, either because they were referred to by word of mouth, found it through personal investigation, or were hired to look into it. Each portion wants something different from the others: the Mediums want to help people, both for the good feelings and because it makes them feel like their supernatural gifts have a purpose; the Investigators want to get paid and to draw attention to the supernatural; and the Parapsychologists want to prove to the academic world that their ideas were right and not just superstitious nonsense. Naturally, this causes tension to occur, especially if those desires come into direct conflict, but the fact that the average Joe and Jane considers the group to made of con artists and crazies, the Compact maintains it's unity.<br /> <br /> Also, now that I think about it, while I drew inspiration for Ecto-Zone from <i>Ghostbusters</i> (Paramount, not Filemation) and <i>Ghost Whisperer </i>(with a little Fatal Frame mixed in as a style merit), the idea of three very different individuals (or groups) working together to fight a supernatural force in a haunted location reminds me of Koudelka (and if anyone here knows what that is, I'll be very happy).<br /> <br /> <b>The Howling Moon Theatre</b>: Mostly likely, the binding performance would cause the spirit/ghost to slowly lose Essense over the course of it, and once its Essence reaches zero it gets bound. Obviously, I'll have to look more into the rules before settling on the idea. I also think that the origin of their performances comes from ancient religious ceremonies that they've adapted to suit more modern theater performances. Also... I'm thinking Wolf-Blooded were involved at some point...<br /> <br /> <b>The Neo Ground Railroad</b>: Yeah... The more I think about it, the more I realize this group probably doesn't work as a playable group. The idea would probably be better represented by making a variant group of Habibti Ma. Plus, the base idea is too passive, since it relies on people coming to them first, and I feel Hunters are suppose to be Pro-Active in their dealings with monsters.<br /> <br /> <b>Unusual Investigations</b>: ...I'm gonna need you to elaborate a bit more on this one, Arcane Arts. I mean, I understand most of what you're saying, and that it was <b>DEFINITELY</b> a problem with the NGR (and also applies to a Conspiracy I tried to create on a different thread...) I'm just not sure I see how it applies to Unusual Investigations. The idea of Unusual Investigations is that they're a detective agency that often finds itself investigating the supernatural. Did I accidentally make them sound more knowing than I intended them to be?<br /> <br /> Also, forgive my ignorance, but I have no idea what STV stands for. I'm guessing Story Teller something that starts with a V.<br /> <br /> <b>Ancestral Wardens</b>: JoJo's Bizarre Ancestory.com was actually pretty much what I was going for, though I doubt the actual Conspiracy know this. Though I'm imagining a member posing as they confront Beasts and Heros.<br /> <br /> <b>The Burnt Torch Society</b>: Yeah, their Endowment needs work beyond the concept phase (accept that failing to use it right should give them the Shaken condition); they fight monster to remind them that there is a reason they should fear humans (they fail to grasp that using supernatural powers to do that undermines the message), they fight Heros because they see Heros as denying fear which they find both insulting and insane (Similar to your proposal for how to fix Heros); No, I have never played Alan Wake.<br /> <br /> <b>JDG Cleaning &amp; Fumigation</b>: They aren't Cheiron partially because they don't augment their Hunters with monster pieces, but mostly because I think Orpheus from OWoD was cool and I thought somebody should port them to CoD as a Hunter Conspiracy.<br /> <br /> Any dog needing to vomit could tell you Grass tastes bad.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":17107,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","user":"Mangaholic13","date":". 03-25-2022, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-27T23:55:48-07:00","id":1477568,"title":"","content":"This Great Cult idea ArcaneArts mentioned sounds super interesting! Are they like a super-Conspiracy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T00:24:58-07:00","id":1477569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrueMrMultiverse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169820-share-your-compact-conspiracy-ideas?p=1477568#post1477568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This Great Cult idea ArcaneArts mentioned sounds super interesting! Are they like a super-Conspiracy?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Grand Cult is a notion I was kicking around and might get around to as a STV idea. It's more of an Anti-Conspiracy, in that it does not fight monsters, it supports them.<br /> <br /> The general idea is that, over the time and tides of history, as the cults of monsters collide, cautiously dance around, possibly coordinate, and over time very probably see the fail state of their supernatural pillars, cultists can meet up, share ideas and values that come from <i>why</i> they joined a cult around a monster, and can play to more of what's in common and alike than not. Give that a lot of time and growing pains, and you might eventually get something that plays like a Conspiracy but is a monster cult instead, which for the specific expression of The Grand Cult, has the ambitions to Connect Monstrous Coalitions into larger and more soundly based organizations, work to Increase the Influence and connections of monsters, particularly working them into high level political, commercial, cultural and other such positions, and finally (and the biggest point of contestation with their subscribed patrons) Eliminate the Ignorance of humanity's separation and superiority over monsters- to basically allow the supernatural to act in their rightful place as the rulers of the world.<br /> <br /> Needless to say, they do still often fight monsters as much as they try to elevate them (because monsters have kidded themsleves into thinking the shadows work better for them, silly gods-we-kneel-to), but the general point is still very much that they are not hunters-rather the opposite. The Factions are more or less centered around who they think should lead, roughly grouped into the Lords, those who seem predisposed to the job, the Beasts, your more apocalyptic/social-Darwinist/primal-anarchist flavor, and the Freaks, when the other two are boring because their approaching the problem of modern society from very boring perspectives where the answer is clearly more sideways to the sun.<br /> <br /> Their Endowment is Trickle-Down Monstrosity, which is like Setto or Anthrophagy operated on Idigam logic, in accordance to the scale of your dedication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T00:30:01-07:00","id":1477570,"title":"","content":"That sounds super interesting! They would be perfect as both as antags and as an organisation a PC is part of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T19:30:34-07:00","id":1477607,"title":"","content":"I always had an idea for a small compact consisting of former touchstones and people who've been touched by the supernatural in some personal or helpful way. Eventually these supernatural people disappear resulting in a lot curiosity and desire to find there old friends.<br /> <br /> This resulted in them meeting up and eventually forming a small compact dedicated to figuring out what happened to them and figuring out how the various societies of supernatural works and functions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}